window.CGL_DATA=window.CGL_DATA||{};window.CGL_DATA["CGL-12-OCT-2026-SHIFT-3"]={"id":"CGL-12-OCT-2026-SHIFT-3","title":"CGL 12 OCT 2026 SHIFT 3","order":["REASONING","GK","MATH","ENGLISH"],"marking":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"qualifying":[],"sections":{"REASONING":{"seconds":900,"questions":[{"no":1,"local_id":"50001","quid":"Q1000071081","section":"REASONING","topic":"Coding & Decoding","question":{"en":"If ‘PQR’ is coded as 161718, what will be the code for ‘STU’? [SSC CGL 12/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"यदि ‘PQR’ को 161718 के रूप में कूटबद्ध किया जाता है, तो ‘STU’ का कूट क्या होगा? [SSC CGL 12/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"192021"},"2":{"en":"182021"},"3":{"en":"202122"},"4":{"en":"171819"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"Each letter is replaced by its alphabet position: P = 16, Q = 17, R = 18<br>STU gives S = 19, T = 20, U = 21<br>Code = 192021<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): 192021.</b>","hi":"प्रत्येक अक्षर को उसके वर्णमाला क्रम से बदला जाता है: P = 16, Q = 17, R = 18<br>STU = S = 19, T = 20, U = 21<br>कूट = 192021<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (1): 192021 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":2,"local_id":"50002","quid":"Q1000071082","section":"REASONING","topic":"Statement & Conclusion","question":{"en":"Read the following statement carefully and identify the conclusion that follows.<br><br><b>Statement:</b> The government made Aadhaar mandatory for all subsidy schemes.<br><b>Conclusions:</b><br>I. People without Aadhaar may lose benefits.<br>II. The government wants to identify all beneficiaries. [SSC CGL 12/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"निम्नलिखित कथन को ध्यान से पढ़िए और वह निष्कर्ष पहचानिए जो अनुसरण करता है।<br><br><b>कथन:</b> सरकार ने सभी सब्सिडी योजनाओं के लिए आधार को अनिवार्य कर दिया।<br><b>निष्कर्ष:</b><br>I. आधार न रखने वाले लोग लाभ खो सकते हैं।<br>II. सरकार सभी लाभार्थियों की पहचान करना चाहती है। [SSC CGL 12/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Only Conclusion I follows","hi":"केवल निष्कर्ष I अनुसरण करता है"},"2":{"en":"Only Conclusion II follows","hi":"केवल निष्कर्ष II अनुसरण करता है"},"3":{"en":"Both I and II follow","hi":"I और II दोनों अनुसरण करते हैं"},"4":{"en":"Neither I nor II follows","hi":"न तो I और न ही II अनुसरण करता है"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"Aadhaar being compulsory for subsidies means no Aadhaar means no subsidy, so I follows<br>Making identity number compulsory is done to identify the beneficiaries, so II follows<br>Both conclusions follow<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): Both I and II follow.</b>","hi":"सब्सिडी के लिए आधार अनिवार्य होने का अर्थ है आधार न हो तो सब्सिडी नहीं, अतः I अनुसरण करता है<br>पहचान संख्या अनिवार्य करने का उद्देश्य लाभार्थियों की पहचान है, अतः II अनुसरण करता है<br>दोनों निष्कर्ष अनुसरण करते हैं<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (3): I और II दोनों अनुसरण करते हैं है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":3,"local_id":"50003","quid":"Q1000071083","section":"REASONING","topic":"Letter & Alphanumeric Series","question":{"en":"Complete the below sequence of letters.<br><br>A, C, E, G, ? [SSC CGL 12/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"अक्षरों की नीचे दी गई श्रेणी को पूरा कीजिए।<br><br>A, C, E, G, ? [SSC CGL 12/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"H"},"2":{"en":"J"},"3":{"en":"I"},"4":{"en":"K"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"Every term jumps two letters forward: A, C, E, G<br>Next letter = I<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): I.</b>","hi":"प्रत्येक पद दो अक्षर आगे बढ़ता है: A, C, E, G<br>अगला अक्षर = I<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (3): I है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":4,"local_id":"50004","quid":"Q1000071084","section":"REASONING","topic":"Coding & Decoding","question":{"en":"If ‘BOOK’ is coded as ‘2-15-15-11’, how is ‘PAGE’ coded? [SSC CGL 12/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"यदि ‘BOOK’ को ‘2-15-15-11’ के रूप में कूटबद्ध किया जाता है, तो ‘PAGE’ कैसे कूटबद्ध होगा? [SSC CGL 12/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"16-2-7-5"},"2":{"en":"16-1-6-5"},"3":{"en":"15-1-7-5"},"4":{"en":"16-1-7-5"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"Every letter is replaced by its alphabet position: B = 2, O = 15, O = 15, K = 11<br>PAGE gives P = 16, A = 1, G = 7, E = 5<br>Code = 16-1-7-5<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): 16-1-7-5.</b>","hi":"प्रत्येक अक्षर को उसके वर्णमाला क्रम से बदला जाता है: B = 2, O = 15, O = 15, K = 11<br>PAGE = P = 16, A = 1, G = 7, E = 5<br>कूट = 16-1-7-5<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (4): 16-1-7-5 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":5,"local_id":"50005","quid":"Q1000071085","section":"REASONING","topic":"Venn Diagrams","question":{"en":"In a group of 40 children, 28 like Ice Cream, 18 like Cake, and 10 like both. How many like only Cake? [SSC CGL 12/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"40 बच्चों के एक समूह में 28 आइसक्रीम पसंद करते हैं, 18 केक पसंद करते हैं और 10 दोनों पसंद करते हैं। कितने बच्चे केवल केक पसंद करते हैं? [SSC CGL 12/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"8"},"2":{"en":"10"},"3":{"en":"5"},"4":{"en":"6"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"Only Cake = Cake − both = 18 − 10 = 8<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): 8.</b>","hi":"केवल केक = केक − दोनों = 18 − 10 = 8<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (1): 8 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":6,"local_id":"50006","quid":"Q1000071086","section":"REASONING","topic":"Venn Diagrams","question":{"en":"In a school, 100 students were surveyed: 60 play Badminton, 50 play Tennis, 40 play Chess, 30 play both Badminton and Tennis, 20 play Tennis and Chess, 15 play Badminton and Chess, 10 play all three. How many play only Chess? [SSC CGL 12/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"एक विद्यालय में 100 विद्यार्थियों का सर्वेक्षण किया गया: 60 बैडमिंटन खेलते हैं, 50 टेनिस, 40 शतरंज, 30 बैडमिंटन और टेनिस दोनों, 20 टेनिस और शतरंज, 15 बैडमिंटन और शतरंज, 10 तीनों खेलते हैं। कितने विद्यार्थी केवल शतरंज खेलते हैं? [SSC CGL 12/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"15"},"2":{"en":"18"},"3":{"en":"20"},"4":{"en":"22"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"Only Chess = 40 − (15 − 10) − (20 − 10) − 10<br>= 40 − 5 − 10 − 10 = 15<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): 15.</b>","hi":"केवल शतरंज = 40 − (15 − 10) − (20 − 10) − 10<br>= 40 − 5 − 10 − 10 = 15<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (1): 15 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":7,"local_id":"50007","quid":"Q1000071087","section":"REASONING","topic":"Miscellaneous","question":{"en":"Solve<br>If 5x − 3y = 27 and x + 2y = 12, what are the values of x and y? [SSC CGL 12/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"हल कीजिए<br>यदि 5x − 3y = 27 और x + 2y = 12 है, तो x और y के मान क्या हैं? [SSC CGL 12/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"x = 6.92, y = 2.54"},"2":{"en":"x = 3.62, y = 4.5"},"3":{"en":"x = 7.2, y = 2.5"},"4":{"en":"x = 5.5, y = 3.5"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"From \\(x + 2y = 12\\), \\(x = 12 - 2y\\)<br>Substituting: \\(5(12 - 2y) - 3y = 27 \\Rightarrow 60 - 13y = 27 \\Rightarrow y = \\frac{33}{13} = 2.54\\)<br>\\(x = 12 - 2(2.54) = 6.92\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): x = 6.92, y = 2.54.</b>","hi":"\\(x + 2y = 12\\) से \\(x = 12 - 2y\\)<br>रखने पर: \\(5(12 - 2y) - 3y = 27 \\Rightarrow 60 - 13y = 27 \\Rightarrow y = \\frac{33}{13} = 2.54\\)<br>\\(x = 12 - 2(2.54) = 6.92\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (1): x = 6.92, y = 2.54 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":8,"local_id":"50008","quid":"Q1000071088","section":"REASONING","topic":"Letter/Alphabetical Analogy","question":{"en":"In the following question, two groups of letters are related by a specific pattern. Identify the same pattern and apply it to the second group to find the missing letters.<br>WXYZ : DJFL :: ABCD : ? [SSC CGL 12/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"निम्नलिखित प्रश्न में अक्षरों के दो समूह एक विशिष्ट पैटर्न से संबंधित हैं। वही पैटर्न पहचानिए और दूसरे समूह पर लागू करके लुप्त अक्षर ज्ञात कीजिए।<br>WXYZ : DJFL :: ABCD : ? [SSC CGL 12/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"HRMX"},"2":{"en":"HLQV"},"3":{"en":"HMSX"},"4":{"en":"HNJP"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"Each letter is replaced by the letter opposite to it: W → D, X → E, Y → F, Z → G, and the last pair shifts by one<br>ABCD gives A → H, B → N, C → J, D → P<br>Code = HNJP<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): HNJP.</b>","hi":"प्रत्येक अक्षर को उसके विपरीत अक्षर से बदला जाता है: W → D, X → E, Y → F, Z → G<br>ABCD से A → H, B → N, C → J, D → P<br>कूट = HNJP<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (4): HNJP है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":9,"local_id":"50009","quid":"Q1000071089","section":"REASONING","topic":"Odd One Out","question":{"en":"In this following question, four words have been given, out of which three are alike in some manner and the fourth one is different. Choose odd one out. [SSC CGL 12/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"इस प्रश्न में चार शब्द दिए गए हैं, जिनमें तीन किसी प्रकार एक जैसे हैं और चौथा भिन्न है। विषम शब्द चुनिए। [SSC CGL 12/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"President","hi":"राष्ट्रपति"},"2":{"en":"Governor","hi":"राज्यपाल"},"3":{"en":"Mayor","hi":"महापौर"},"4":{"en":"Prime Minister","hi":"प्रधानमंत्री"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"President, Governor and Prime Minister are heads at the national or state level<br>A Mayor heads only a city corporation, which is a local body<br>So Mayor is the odd one<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): Mayor.</b>","hi":"राष्ट्रपति, राज्यपाल और प्रधानमंत्री राष्ट्रीय या राज्य स्तर के प्रमुख हैं<br>महापौर केवल नगर निगम का प्रमुख होता है, जो स्थानीय निकाय है<br>अतः महापौर विषम है<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (3): महापौर है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":10,"local_id":"50010","quid":"Q1000071090","section":"REASONING","topic":"Address/Sentence Matching","question":{"en":"Choose the option that perfectly matches the given address.<br><br><b>Original Address:</b><br>Suite 18/B-09King’s Landing Residency, Phase–XIIMahatma Gandhi Rd. ExtensionHyderabad, Telangana 500081India [SSC CGL 12/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"वह विकल्प चुनिए जो दिए गए पते से पूर्णतः मेल खाता है।<br><br><b>मूल पता:</b><br>Suite 18/B-09King’s Landing Residency, Phase–XIIMahatma Gandhi Rd. ExtensionHyderabad, Telangana 500081India [SSC CGL 12/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Suite 18/B-09King’s Landing Residency, Phase–XIIMahatma Gandhi Road ExtensionHyderabad, Telangana 500081India"},"2":{"en":"Suite 18/B-09King’s Landing Residency, Phase–XIIIMahatma Gandhi Rd. ExtensionHyderabad, Telangana 500081India"},"3":{"en":"Suite 18/B-09King’s Landing Residency, Phase–XIIMahatma Gandhi Rd. ExtensionHyderabad, Telangana 500018India"},"4":{"en":"Suite 18/B-09King’s Landing Residency, Phase–XIIMahatma Gandhi Rd. ExtensionHyderabad, Telangana 500081India"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"Option 1 writes Gandhi Road instead of Gandhi Rd., option 2 changes Phase–XII to Phase–XIII, option 3 changes the PIN to 500018<br>Option 4 keeps Phase–XII, Rd. and 500081 exactly as printed<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): Suite 18/B-09King’s Landing Residency, Phase–XIIMahatma Gandhi Rd. ExtensionHyderabad, Telangana 500081India.</b>","hi":"विकल्प 1 में Gandhi Rd. के स्थान पर Gandhi Road है, विकल्प 2 में Phase–XII के स्थान पर Phase–XIII है, विकल्प 3 में पिन 500018 है<br>विकल्प 4 में Phase–XII, Rd. तथा 500081 ठीक वैसे ही हैं<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (4): Suite 18/B-09King’s Landing Residency, Phase–XIIMahatma Gandhi Rd. ExtensionHyderabad, Telangana 500081India है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":11,"local_id":"50011","quid":"Q1000071091","section":"REASONING","topic":"Counting Figures","question":{"en":"How many squares are there in the given figure?<br><img src=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-12-OCT-2026-SHIFT-3/q11.jpg\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\"> [SSC CGL 12/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"दी गई आकृति में कितने वर्ग हैं?<br><img src=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-12-OCT-2026-SHIFT-3/q11.jpg\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\"> [SSC CGL 12/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"35"},"2":{"en":"47"},"3":{"en":"51"},"4":{"en":"55"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"The figure is a 5 × 5 grid of small squares<br>1 × 1 squares = 25, 2 × 2 = 16, 3 × 3 = 9, 4 × 4 = 4, 5 × 5 = 1<br>Total = 25 + 16 + 9 + 4 + 1 = 55<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): 55.</b>","hi":"आकृति 5 × 5 छोटे वर्गों का जाल है<br>1 × 1 वर्ग = 25, 2 × 2 = 16, 3 × 3 = 9, 4 × 4 = 4, 5 × 5 = 1<br>कुल = 25 + 16 + 9 + 4 + 1 = 55<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (4): 55 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":true,"images":{"question":["https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-12-OCT-2026-SHIFT-3/q11.jpg"]}},{"no":12,"local_id":"50012","quid":"Q1000071092","section":"REASONING","topic":"Word Formation & Letter/Word Position","question":{"en":"How many such letters are there in the word SECURE, which are in the same position as in the English alphabet? [SSC CGL 12/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"शब्द SECURE में ऐसे कितने अक्षर हैं, जो अंग्रेज़ी वर्णमाला में अपने ही स्थान पर हैं? [SSC CGL 12/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"1"},"2":{"en":"2"},"3":{"en":"3"},"4":{"en":"4"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"S = 19, E = 5, C = 3, U = 21, R = 18, E = 5<br>Comparing with positions in the word, only the third letter C matches its alphabet position 3<br>Count = 1<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): 1.</b>","hi":"S = 19, E = 5, C = 3, U = 21, R = 18, E = 5<br>शब्द में स्थान से तुलना करने पर केवल तीसरा अक्षर C अपने वर्णमाला क्रम 3 पर है<br>संख्या = 1<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (1): 1 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":13,"local_id":"50013","quid":"Q1000071093","section":"REASONING","topic":"Letter & Alphanumeric Series","question":{"en":"Study the pattern in the given series and find the next set of letters in the series.<br>CHI, EGK, GFM, ? [SSC CGL 12/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"दी गई श्रेणी का पैटर्न अध्ययन कीजिए और अक्षरों का अगला समूह ज्ञात कीजिए।<br>CHI, EGK, GFM, ? [SSC CGL 12/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"IEO"},"2":{"en":"IOE"},"3":{"en":"IDP"},"4":{"en":"IEP"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"First letters C, E, G go 2 forward, so next is I<br>Second letters H, G, F go 1 back, so next is E<br>Third letters I, K, M go 2 forward, so next is O<br>Next group = IEO<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): IEO.</b>","hi":"पहले अक्षर C, E, G हर बार 2 आगे, अतः अगला I<br>दूसरे अक्षर H, G, F हर बार 1 पीछे, अतः अगला E<br>तीसरे अक्षर I, K, M हर बार 2 आगे, अतः अगला O<br>अगला समूह = IEO<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (1): IEO है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":14,"local_id":"50014","quid":"Q1000071094","section":"REASONING","topic":"Figure Completing","question":{"en":"Complete the pattern in fig. (X) by selecting one of the figures from the four alternatives :<br>Figure(X):<br><img src=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-12-OCT-2026-SHIFT-3/q14.jpg\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\"> [SSC CGL 12/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"आकृति (X) का पैटर्न चार विकल्पों में से एक आकृति चुनकर पूरा कीजिए :<br>आकृति (X):<br><img src=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-12-OCT-2026-SHIFT-3/q14.jpg\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\"> [SSC CGL 12/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{},"2":{},"3":{},"4":{}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"Figure (X) is the arrow with the shaded blocks inside it; the answer keeps the same block pattern while the arrow turns<br>Only the figure in option 2 carries the identical pattern of shaded parts<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): <img src=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-12-OCT-2026-SHIFT-3/q14_opt2.jpg\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\">.</b>","hi":"आकृति (X) श्रेणी में तीर है जिसके भीतर छायांकित खंड हैं; उत्तर में वही खंड-पैटर्न रहता है और तीर घूम जाता है<br>केवल विकल्प 2 की आकृति में छायांकित भागों का वही पैटर्न है<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): <img src=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-12-OCT-2026-SHIFT-3/q14_opt2.jpg\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\"> है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":true,"images":{"question":["https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-12-OCT-2026-SHIFT-3/q14.jpg"],"options":{"1":["https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-12-OCT-2026-SHIFT-3/q14_opt1.jpg"],"2":["https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-12-OCT-2026-SHIFT-3/q14_opt2.jpg"],"3":["https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-12-OCT-2026-SHIFT-3/q14_opt3.jpg"],"4":["https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-12-OCT-2026-SHIFT-3/q14_opt4.jpg"]},"solution":["https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-12-OCT-2026-SHIFT-3/q14_opt2.jpg"]}},{"no":15,"local_id":"50015","quid":"Q1000071095","section":"REASONING","topic":"Mathematical Operations","question":{"en":"Which two signs and two numbers need to be interchanged to make the given equation correct?<br>16 − 4 × 6 ÷ 2 + 8 = 20 [SSC CGL 12/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"दिए गए समीकरण को सही बनाने के लिए किन दो चिह्नों तथा दो संख्याओं को परस्पर बदलना होगा?<br>16 − 4 × 6 ÷ 2 + 8 = 20 [SSC CGL 12/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Interchange + and −, and numbers 4 and 6","hi":"+ और − तथा संख्याएँ 4 और 6 बदलें"},"2":{"en":"Interchange × and ÷, and numbers 6 and 8","hi":"× और ÷ तथा संख्याएँ 6 और 8 बदलें"},"3":{"en":"Interchange − and ÷, and numbers 16 and 6","hi":"− और ÷ तथा संख्याएँ 16 और 6 बदलें"},"4":{"en":"Interchange ÷ and +, and numbers 4 and 8","hi":"÷ और + तथा संख्याएँ 4 और 8 बदलें"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"After interchanging + and − and also 4 and 6: 16 + 6 × 4 ÷ 2 − 8<br>= 16 + 12 − 8 = 20 ✔<br>Only option 1 gives the correct value<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): Interchange + and −, and numbers 4 and 6.</b>","hi":"+ और − तथा 4 और 6 बदलने पर: 16 + 6 × 4 ÷ 2 − 8<br>= 16 + 12 − 8 = 20 ✔<br>केवल विकल्प 1 सही मान देता है<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (1): + और − तथा संख्याएँ 4 और 6 बदलें है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":16,"local_id":"50016","quid":"Q1000071096","section":"REASONING","topic":"Situational Judgement","question":{"en":"While preparing a quarterly report, you find that a minor data error from a previous month made the current figures look better than they actually are. Your manager is already planning to present these results to senior leadership today. What should you do? [SSC CGL 12/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"त्रैमासिक रिपोर्ट तैयार करते समय आप पाते हैं कि पिछले महीने की एक छोटी डेटा त्रुटि के कारण वर्तमान आँकड़े वास्तविकता से बेहतर दिख रहे हैं। आपका प्रबंधक आज ही ये परिणाम वरिष्ठ नेतृत्व के सामने प्रस्तुत करने की योजना बना रहा है। आपको क्या करना चाहिए? [SSC CGL 12/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Keep silent since the error was made by someone else and the current results are positive.","hi":"चुप रहें, क्योंकि त्रुटि किसी और ने की थी और वर्तमान परिणाम सकारात्मक हैं।"},"2":{"en":"Inform your manager and provide a corrected version before the meeting.","hi":"प्रबंधक को सूचित करें और बैठक से पहले सुधरा हुआ संस्करण दें।"},"3":{"en":"Fix the error silently after the meeting if anyone asks for clarification.","hi":"यदि बैठक के बाद कोई स्पष्टीकरण माँगे तो चुपचाप त्रुटि सुधार दें।"},"4":{"en":"Delete the report and claim you lost the file to buy more time.","hi":"रिपोर्ट हटा दें और समय बचाने के लिए कहें कि फ़ाइल खो गई है।"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"Wrong data must not reach senior leadership<br>Informing the manager with a corrected version before the meeting protects both the report and the team's credibility<br>Silence or deletion turns a small error into a trust issue<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): Inform your manager and provide a corrected version before the meeting.</b>","hi":"गलत आँकड़े वरिष्ठ नेतृत्व तक नहीं पहुँचने चाहिए<br>बैठक से पहले प्रबंधक को बताकर सुधरा संस्करण देना रिपोर्ट तथा टीम दोनों की विश्वसनीयता बचाता है<br>चुप रहना या फ़ाइल हटाना छोटी त्रुटि को विश्वास की समस्या बना देता है<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): प्रबंधक को सूचित करें और बैठक से पहले सुधरा हुआ संस्करण दें। है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":17,"local_id":"50017","quid":"Q1000071097","section":"REASONING","topic":"Embedded Figures","question":{"en":"In the following question, a figure (X) is given, followed by four alternative figures (1), (2), (3), and (4) such that figure (X) is embedded in one of them. Trace out the alternative figure that contains fig. (X) as part of it.<br>Figure(X):<br><img src=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-12-OCT-2026-SHIFT-3/q17.jpg\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\"> [SSC CGL 12/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"निम्नलिखित प्रश्न में एक आकृति (X) दी गई है, उसके बाद चार वैकल्पिक आकृतियाँ (1), (2), (3) और (4) हैं, जिनमें आकृति (X) किसी एक में निहित है। वह वैकल्पिक आकृति पहचानिए जिसमें आकृति (X) उसका भाग है।<br>आकृति (X):<br><img src=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-12-OCT-2026-SHIFT-3/q17.jpg\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\"> [SSC CGL 12/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{},"2":{},"3":{},"4":{}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"The arrow-head shape of figure (X) reappears without rotation inside alternative figure 3<br>The other three alternatives change the angles of the shape<br>So the answer is figure 3<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): <img src=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-12-OCT-2026-SHIFT-3/q17_opt2.jpg\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\">.</b>","hi":"आकृति (X) का तीर-शीर्ष आकार बिना घुमाए वैकल्पिक आकृति 3 के भीतर मिलता है<br>शेष तीन आकृतियाँ आकार के कोण बदल देती हैं<br>अतः उत्तर आकृति 3 है<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): <img src=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-12-OCT-2026-SHIFT-3/q17_opt2.jpg\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\"> है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":true,"images":{"question":["https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-12-OCT-2026-SHIFT-3/q17.jpg"],"options":{"1":["https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-12-OCT-2026-SHIFT-3/q17_opt1.jpg"],"2":["https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-12-OCT-2026-SHIFT-3/q17_opt2.jpg"],"3":["https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-12-OCT-2026-SHIFT-3/q17_opt3.jpg"],"4":["https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-12-OCT-2026-SHIFT-3/q17_opt4.jpg"]},"solution":["https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-12-OCT-2026-SHIFT-3/q17_opt2.jpg"]}},{"no":18,"local_id":"50018","quid":"Q1000071098","section":"REASONING","topic":"Statement, Assumption & Argument","question":{"en":"Read the given statement carefully and the following assumptions based on it. Decide which of the assumptions are implicit in the statement.<br><b>Statement:</b><br>Many schools are introducing mandatory coding classes in their curriculum to prepare students for a future dominated by technology.<br><b>Assumptions:</b><br>I. Proficiency in coding will be a vital skill for the future job market.<br>II. Traditional subjects taught in schools are no longer relevant for the modern student. [SSC CGL 12/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"दिया गया कथन ध्यान से पढ़िए और उस पर आधारित अनुमानों को देखिए। निर्णय कीजिए कि कौन-से अनुमान कथन में निहित हैं।<br><b>कथन:</b><br>कई विद्यालय तकनीक से संचालित भविष्य के लिए विद्यार्थियों को तैयार करने हेतु अपने पाठ्यक्रम में अनिवार्य कोडिंग कक्षाएँ शुरू कर रहे हैं।<br><b>अनुमान:</b><br>I. कोडिंग में दक्षता भविष्य के रोजगार बाज़ार के लिए एक महत्वपूर्ण कौशल होगी।<br>II. विद्यालयों में पढ़ाए जाने वाले पारंपरिक विषय आधुनिक विद्यार्थी के लिए अब प्रासंगिक नहीं हैं। [SSC CGL 12/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Only Assumption I is implicit","hi":"केवल अनुमान I निहित है"},"2":{"en":"Only Assumption II is implicit","hi":"केवल अनुमान II निहित है"},"3":{"en":"Both Assumptions I and II are implicit","hi":"अनुमान I और II दोनों निहित हैं"},"4":{"en":"Neither Assumption I nor II is implicit","hi":"न तो अनुमान I और न ही II निहित है"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"Coding is made compulsory because it is expected to be a vital skill, so I is implicit<br>Nothing in the statement says traditional subjects have lost relevance, so II is not implicit<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): Only Assumption I is implicit.</b>","hi":"कोडिंग अनिवार्य इसलिए की गई क्योंकि वह महत्वपूर्ण कौशल मानी गई है, अतः I निहित है<br>कथन में पारंपरिक विषयों की अप्रासंगिकता का कोई संकेत नहीं, अतः II निहित नहीं है<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (1): केवल अनुमान I निहित है है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":19,"local_id":"50019","quid":"Q1000071099","section":"REASONING","topic":"Odd One Out","question":{"en":"In the following question, out of the five figures marked (a), (b), (c), (d), and (e), four are similar in a certain manner. However, one figure is not like the other four. Choose the figure which is different from the rest.<br><img src=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-12-OCT-2026-SHIFT-3/q19.jpg\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\"> [SSC CGL 12/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"निम्नलिखित प्रश्न में (a), (b), (c), (d) और (e) से अंकित पाँच आकृतियों में से चार किसी प्रकार एक जैसी हैं। परंतु एक आकृति शेष चारों जैसी नहीं है। वह आकृति चुनिए जो शेष से भिन्न है।<br><img src=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-12-OCT-2026-SHIFT-3/q19.jpg\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\"> [SSC CGL 12/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"d"},"2":{"en":"a"},"3":{"en":"b"},"4":{"en":"c"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"In (a), (b), (c) and (e) a figure is enclosed inside another one of a different type<br>In (d) two triangles of the same shape are placed one inside the other<br>So (d) is the different figure<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): d.</b>","hi":"(a), (b), (c) और (e) में एक आकृति दूसरे प्रकार की आकृति के भीतर है<br>(d) में एक ही आकार के दो त्रिभुज एक-दूसरे के भीतर हैं<br>अतः (d) भिन्न आकृति है<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (1): d है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":true,"images":{"question":["https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-12-OCT-2026-SHIFT-3/q19.jpg"]}},{"no":20,"local_id":"50020","quid":"Q1000071100","section":"REASONING","topic":"Counting Figures","question":{"en":"How many triangles are there in the given figure?<br><img src=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-12-OCT-2026-SHIFT-3/q20.jpg\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\"> [SSC CGL 12/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"दी गई आकृति में कितने त्रिभुज हैं?<br><img src=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-12-OCT-2026-SHIFT-3/q20.jpg\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\"> [SSC CGL 12/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"36"},"2":{"en":"40"},"3":{"en":"44"},"4":{"en":"48"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"Outer square with both diagonals gives 16 triangles<br>The inscribed square standing on the midpoints adds 16 more<br>The innermost square with its two diagonals adds another 16<br>Total = 16 + 16 + 16 = 48<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): 48.</b>","hi":"दोनों विकर्णों वाला बाहरी वर्ग 16 त्रिभुज देता है<br>भुजाओं के मध्य-बिंदुओं पर बना भीतरी वर्ग 16 और जोड़ता है<br>सबसे भीतरी वर्ग अपने दोनों विकर्णों सहित 16 और जोड़ता है<br>कुल = 16 + 16 + 16 = 48<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (4): 48 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":true,"images":{"question":["https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-12-OCT-2026-SHIFT-3/q20.jpg"]}},{"no":21,"local_id":"50021","quid":"Q1000071101","section":"REASONING","topic":"Figure Series & Figure Analogy","question":{"en":"In the following question, there is a specific relationship between the first two figures. Establish a similar relationship between the third and fourth figures by selecting a suitable figure from the given Answer Figures to replace the question mark (?).<br>Question Figures:<br><img src=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-12-OCT-2026-SHIFT-3/q21.jpg\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\"> [SSC CGL 12/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"निम्नलिखित प्रश्न में पहली दो आकृतियों के बीच एक विशिष्ट संबंध है। तीसरी और चौथी आकृति के बीच वही संबंध स्थापित करने के लिए दी गई उत्तर आकृतियों में से उपयुक्त आकृति चुनकर प्रश्नवाचक चिह्न (?) के स्थान पर रखिए।<br>प्रश्न आकृतियाँ:<br><img src=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-12-OCT-2026-SHIFT-3/q21.jpg\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\"> [SSC CGL 12/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{},"2":{},"3":{},"4":{}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"In the first pair the whole figure turns 180° and the small circle moves from the bottom right to the left<br>Applying the same turn and shift to the third figure gives answer figure 3<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): <img src=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-12-OCT-2026-SHIFT-3/q21_opt2.jpg\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\">.</b>","hi":"पहले युग्म में पूरी आकृति 180° घूम जाती है और छोटा वृत्त नीचे दाईं ओर से बाईं ओर चला जाता है<br>तीसरी आकृति पर वही घूर्णन और स्थानांतरण लगाने पर उत्तर आकृति 3 मिलती है<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): <img src=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-12-OCT-2026-SHIFT-3/q17_opt2.jpg\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\"> है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":true,"images":{"question":["https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-12-OCT-2026-SHIFT-3/q21.jpg"],"options":{"1":["https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-12-OCT-2026-SHIFT-3/q21_opt1.jpg"],"2":["https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-12-OCT-2026-SHIFT-3/q21_opt2.jpg"],"3":["https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-12-OCT-2026-SHIFT-3/q21_opt3.jpg"],"4":["https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-12-OCT-2026-SHIFT-3/q21_opt4.jpg"]},"solution":["https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-12-OCT-2026-SHIFT-3/q21_opt2.jpg","https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-12-OCT-2026-SHIFT-3/q17_opt2.jpg"]}},{"no":22,"local_id":"50022","quid":"Q1000071102","section":"REASONING","topic":"Figure Series & Figure Analogy","question":{"en":"In the following question, there is a specific relationship between the first two figures. Establish a similar relationship between the third and fourth figures by selecting a suitable figure from the given Answer Figures to replace the question mark (?).<br>Question Figures:<br><img src=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-12-OCT-2026-SHIFT-3/q22.jpg\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\"> [SSC CGL 12/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"निम्नलिखित प्रश्न में पहली दो आकृतियों के बीच एक विशिष्ट संबंध है। तीसरी और चौथी आकृति के बीच वही संबंध स्थापित करने के लिए दी गई उत्तर आकृतियों में से उपयुक्त आकृति चुनकर प्रश्नवाचक चिह्न (?) के स्थान पर रखिए।<br>प्रश्न आकृतियाँ:<br><img src=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-12-OCT-2026-SHIFT-3/q22.jpg\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\"> [SSC CGL 12/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{},"2":{},"3":{},"4":{}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"In (A) → (B) the outer pentagon turns upside down and the small dark ellipse moves to the top with the circle below it<br>Doing the same to (C) gives answer figure 1<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): <img src=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-12-OCT-2026-SHIFT-3/q22_opt1.jpg\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\">.</b>","hi":"(A) → (B) में बाहरी पंचभुज उलट जाता है और छोटा गहरा अंडाकार ऊपर चला जाता है, नीचे वृत्त रहता है<br>(C) पर वही करने से उत्तर आकृति 1 मिलती है<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (1): <img src=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-12-OCT-2026-SHIFT-3/q21_opt1.jpg\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\"> है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":true,"images":{"question":["https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-12-OCT-2026-SHIFT-3/q22.jpg"],"options":{"1":["https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-12-OCT-2026-SHIFT-3/q22_opt1.jpg"],"2":["https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-12-OCT-2026-SHIFT-3/q22_opt2.jpg"],"3":["https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-12-OCT-2026-SHIFT-3/q22_opt3.jpg"],"4":["https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-12-OCT-2026-SHIFT-3/q22_opt4.jpg"]},"solution":["https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-12-OCT-2026-SHIFT-3/q22_opt1.jpg","https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-12-OCT-2026-SHIFT-3/q21_opt1.jpg"]}},{"no":23,"local_id":"50023","quid":"Q1000071103","section":"REASONING","topic":"Letter & Alphanumeric Series","question":{"en":"Fill in the blanks (_) using one of the following four options such that the series follows a specific pattern in the given order.<br>cc_c cbc_acc bcc_c_b [SSC CGL 12/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"दिए गए चार विकल्पों में से एक का प्रयोग करके रिक्त स्थान (_) भरिए ताकि श्रेणी दिए गए क्रम में एक विशिष्ट पैटर्न का पालन करे।<br>cc_c cbc_acc bcc_c_b [SSC CGL 12/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"abac"},"2":{"en":"acac"},"3":{"en":"aabc"},"4":{"en":"acba"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"The series repeats the blocks cbc, cac and cbc<br>Filling with a, c, a, c gives ccac cbcac c bccacb, which reads as the repeating block c a c b<br>Only the option acac keeps the pattern unbroken<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): acac.</b>","hi":"श्रेणी cbc, cac और cbc खंडों को दोहराती है<br>a, c, a, c भरने पर ccac cbcac c bccacb बनता है, जो c a c b खंड को दोहराता है<br>केवल विकल्प acac पैटर्न को अखंड रखता है<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): acac है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":24,"local_id":"50024","quid":"Q1000071104","section":"REASONING","topic":"Embedded Figures","question":{"en":"Carefully observe Figure (X) and identify the answer figure in which Figure (X) is embedded in the same or rotated form.<br>Figure X:<br><img src=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-12-OCT-2026-SHIFT-3/q24.jpg\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\"> [SSC CGL 12/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"आकृति (X) को ध्यान से देखिए और वह उत्तर आकृति पहचानिए जिसमें आकृति (X) उसी या घुमाए हुए रूप में निहित है।<br>आकृति X:<br><img src=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-12-OCT-2026-SHIFT-3/q24.jpg\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\"> [SSC CGL 12/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{},"2":{},"3":{},"4":{}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"The zig-zag path of figure (X) appears inside answer figure 4<br>The other figures change the angles of that path<br>So the answer is figure 4<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): <img src=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-12-OCT-2026-SHIFT-3/q24_opt2.jpg\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\">.</b>","hi":"आकृति (X) का टेढ़ा-मेढ़ा पथ उत्तर आकृति 4 के भीतर मिलता है<br>शेष आकृतियाँ उस पथ के कोण बदल देती हैं<br>अतः उत्तर आकृति 4 है<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): <img src=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-12-OCT-2026-SHIFT-3/q21_opt4.jpg\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\"> है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":true,"images":{"question":["https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-12-OCT-2026-SHIFT-3/q24.jpg"],"options":{"1":["https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-12-OCT-2026-SHIFT-3/q17_opt1.jpg"],"2":["https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-12-OCT-2026-SHIFT-3/q24_opt2.jpg"],"3":["https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-12-OCT-2026-SHIFT-3/q24_opt3.jpg"],"4":["https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-12-OCT-2026-SHIFT-3/q17_opt2.jpg"]},"solution":["https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-12-OCT-2026-SHIFT-3/q24_opt2.jpg","https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-12-OCT-2026-SHIFT-3/q21_opt4.jpg"]}},{"no":25,"local_id":"50025","quid":"Q1000071105","section":"REASONING","topic":"Number Series","question":{"en":"Study the following number trend and select the next term:<br><br>14, 21, 33, 52, 80, ? [SSC CGL 12/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"निम्नलिखित संख्या प्रवृत्ति का अध्ययन कीजिए और अगला पद चुनिए:<br><br>14, 21, 33, 52, 80, ? [SSC CGL 12/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"115"},"2":{"en":"117"},"3":{"en":"119"},"4":{"en":"121"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"Differences are 7, 12, 19, 28, which increase by 5, 7, 9<br>Next difference rises by 11, so 28 + 11 = 39<br>Next term = 80 + 39 = 119<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): 119.</b>","hi":"अंतर 7, 12, 19, 28 हैं, जो 5, 7, 9 से बढ़ते हैं<br>अगला अंतर 11 से बढ़ेगा, अतः 28 + 11 = 39<br>अगला पद = 80 + 39 = 119<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (3): 119 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false}]},"GK":{"seconds":900,"questions":[{"no":26,"local_id":"50026","quid":"Q1000071106","section":"GK","topic":"Ancient History: Indus Valley Civilization","question":{"en":"Which highly valued blue stone was procured by the Harappan Civilization from Shortughai in Afghanistan? [SSC CGL 12/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"हड़प्पा सभ्यता द्वारा अफगानिस्तान के शोर्तुघई से कौन-सा अत्यधिक मूल्यवान नीला पत्थर प्राप्त किया जाता था? [SSC CGL 12/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Steatite","hi":"स्टीटाइट"},"2":{"en":"Lapis lazuli","hi":"लापिस लाजुली"},"3":{"en":"Jasper","hi":"जैस्पर"},"4":{"en":"Blue quartz","hi":"नीला क्वार्ट्ज"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (2) – Lapis lazuli</b><br>The Harappans obtained the deep blue semi-precious stone <b>lapis lazuli</b> from <b>Shortughai</b> in the Badakhshan region of north-eastern Afghanistan. It was used for beads and ornaments and shows the long-distance trade network of the civilisation.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• <b>Shortughai</b> was a Harappan trading outpost in Afghanistan, connected with the lapis mines of Badakhshan.<br>• Other raw materials and their sources: <b>steatite</b> from Gujarat and Rajasthan, carnelian from Gujarat (Bharuch), gold from Karnataka (Kolar) and Afghanistan, silver from Iran, copper from Rajasthan (Khetri) and Oman.<br>• Harappan beads were made of carnelian, jasper, shell faience and steatite, and the craft is best seen at <b>Chanhu-daro</b> and Lothal.<br>• The main Harappan ports were <b>Lothal</b> in Gujarat and Sutkagendor and Balakot on the Makran coast, which linked the Indus region with Mesopotamia (Meluhha trade).","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (2) – लापिस लाजुली</b><br>हड़प्पावासी गहरे नीले अर्ध-कीमती पत्थर <b>लापिस लाजुली</b> को उत्तर-पूर्वी अफगानिस्तान के बदख्शां क्षेत्र में स्थित <b>शोर्तुघई</b> से प्राप्त करते थे। इसका उपयोग मनकों व आभूषणों में होता था, जो सभ्यता के दूरगामी व्यापार नेटवर्क को दर्शाता है।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• <b>शोर्तुघई</b> अफगानिस्तान में हड़प्पाई व्यापारिक चौकी थी, जो बदख्शां की लापिस खानों से जुड़ी थी।<br>• अन्य कच्चे माल व उनके स्रोत: <b>स्टीटाइट</b> गुजरात व राजस्थान से, कार्नेलियन गुजरात (भरूच) से, सोना कर्नाटक (कोलार) व अफगानिस्तान से, चाँदी ईरान से, ताँबा राजस्थान (खेतड़ी) व ओमान से।<br>• हड़प्पाई मनके कार्नेलियन, जैस्पर, शंख, फ़ाइंस व स्टीटाइट से बनते थे और यह शिल्प <b>चन्हूदड़ो</b> व लोथल में विशेष रूप से मिलता है।<br>• प्रमुख हड़प्पाई बंदरगाह <b>लोथल</b> (गुजरात) तथा मकरान तट के सुत्कागेंडोर व बालाकोट थे, जो सिंधु क्षेत्र को मेसोपोटामिया (मेलुहा व्यापार) से जोड़ते थे।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":27,"local_id":"50027","quid":"Q1000071107","section":"GK","topic":"Ancient History: Stone Age","question":{"en":"Which of the following is the <b>correct</b> order of Stone Age periods? [SSC CGL 12/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"निम्नलिखित में से पाषाण युग के कालखंडों का <b>सही</b> क्रम कौन-सा है? [SSC CGL 12/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Mesolithic → Palaeolithic → Neolithic","hi":"मध्य पाषाण → पुरा पाषाण → नव पाषाण"},"2":{"en":"Neolithic → Mesolithic → Palaeolithic","hi":"नव पाषाण → मध्य पाषाण → पुरा पाषाण"},"3":{"en":"Palaeolithic → Mesolithic → Neolithic","hi":"पुरा पाषाण → मध्य पाषाण → नव पाषाण"},"4":{"en":"Palaeolithic → Neolithic → Mesolithic","hi":"पुरा पाषाण → नव पाषाण → मध्य पाषाण"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (3) – Palaeolithic → Mesolithic → Neolithic</b><br>The Stone Age developed in the order <b>Palaeolithic (Old Stone Age) → Mesolithic (Middle Stone Age) → Neolithic (New Stone Age)</b>. The Palaeolithic is marked by crude quartzite tools and hunting-gathering, the Mesolithic by microliths, and the Neolithic by polished tools, agriculture and domestication of animals.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• The <b>Palaeolithic</b> (about 5,00,000–10,000 BCE) is divided into lower, middle and upper phases, with sites such as Bhimbetka, Soan valley and Hunsgi.<br>• The <b>Mesolithic</b> (about 9,000–6,000 BCE) is known for microliths, the first rock paintings and sites such as Bagor in Rajasthan and Adamgarh.<br>• The <b>Neolithic</b> (about 7,000–1,000 BCE) brought agriculture (wheat, barley), domestication of cattle, wheel-made pottery and settled village life; <b>Mehrgarh</b> and Burzahom are important sites.<br>• The <b>Chalcolithic</b> (Copper-Stone) Age followed the Neolithic, with the first use of copper tools and painted pottery of the Malwa and Jorwe cultures.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (3) – पुरा पाषाण → मध्य पाषाण → नव पाषाण</b><br>पाषाण युग का विकास इस क्रम में हुआ — <b>पुरा पाषाण → मध्य पाषाण → नव पाषाण</b>। पुरा पाषाण कच्चे क्वार्ट्ज़ाइट उपकरणों तथा शिकार-संग्रह पर आधारित था, मध्य पाषाण सूक्ष्मशिलाओं (microliths) हेतु तथा नव पाषाण पॉलिश किए उपकरणों, कृषि व पशुपालन हेतु जाना जाता है।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• <b>पुरा पाषाण</b> (लगभग 5,00,000–10,000 ईसा पूर्व) अधोत्तर, मध्य व उत्तर चरणों में विभाजित है; भीमबेटका, सोआन घाटी तथा हुनस्गी इसके प्रमुख स्थल हैं।<br>• <b>मध्य पाषाण</b> (लगभग 9,000–6,000 ईसा पूर्व) सूक्ष्मशिलाओं, प्रथम शैलचित्रों तथा राजस्थान के बागोर व आदमगढ़ जैसे स्थलों हेतु प्रसिद्ध है।<br>• <b>नव पाषाण</b> (लगभग 7,000–1,000 ईसा पूर्व) में कृषि (गेहूँ, जौ), पशुपालन, चक्र-निर्मित मृद्भाण्ड तथा स्थायी ग्रामीण जीवन आया; <b>मेहरगढ़</b> व बुर्जहोम महत्वपूर्ण स्थल हैं।<br>• नव पाषाण के बाद <b>ताम्र पाषाण</b> युग आया, जिसमें ताँबे के उपकरण तथा मालवा व जोरवे संस्कृतियों के चित्रित मृद्भाण्ड मिलते हैं।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":28,"local_id":"50028","quid":"Q1000071108","section":"GK","topic":"Medieval History: The Mughal Empire","question":{"en":"Which of the following best describes Khanazad in the Mughal Mansabdari system? [SSC CGL 12/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"मुगल मनसबदारी व्यवस्था में \"खानाज़ाद\" का सर्वोत्तम वर्णन निम्नलिखित में से कौन-सा है? [SSC CGL 12/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Foreign nobles appointed from Central Asia and Persia.","hi":"मध्य एशिया और फारस से नियुक्त विदेशी अमीर।"},"2":{"en":"Sons or close relatives of serving imperial nobles.","hi":"सेवारत शाही अमीरों के पुत्र या निकट संबंधी।"},"3":{"en":"Officers selected through competitive examination.","hi":"प्रतियोगी परीक्षा से चयनित अधिकारी।"},"4":{"en":"Governors appointed from provincial elites.","hi":"प्रांतीय अभिजात वर्ग से नियुक्त गवर्नर।"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (2) – Sons or close relatives of serving imperial nobles.</b><br><b>Khanazad</b> literally means \"house-born\" — the <b>sons and close relatives of serving Mughal nobles</b> who were given mansabs, often at a lower rank than the father, and who formed a hereditary element in the nobility.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• The Mughal nobility had several groups — <b>Khanazad</b> (house-born), <b>Mirzas</b> (Timurid descendants), Indian Muslims, Rajputs and foreign nobles of Irani and Turani origin.<br>• The <b>mansabdari system</b> graded officers by <b>zat</b> (personal rank) and <b>sawar</b> (cavalry rank), and the number of horsemen to be maintained.<br>• The <b>do-aspah-sih-aspah</b> system under Jahangir allowed a noble to maintain double the horses for the same sawar rank in alternate months.<br>• Sher Shah Suri’s reforms in revenue administration, the dagh (branding) system and the rupiya were later adopted and refined by Akbar.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (2) – सेवारत शाही अमीरों के पुत्र या निकट संबंधी।</b><br><b>खानाज़ाद</b> का शाब्दिक अर्थ है \"घर में जन्मा\" — अर्थात् <b>सेवारत मुगल अमीरों के पुत्र व निकट संबंधी</b>, जिन्हें अकसर पिता से निम्न मनसब दिया जाता था और जो अभिजात वर्ग में वंशानुगत तत्व बन गए।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• मुगल अभिजात वर्ग के कई वर्ग थे — <b>खानाज़ाद</b> (घर में जन्मे), <b>मिर्ज़ा</b> (तैमूरी वंशज), भारतीय मुस्लिम, राजपूत तथा ईरानी व तुरानी मूल के विदेशी अमीर।<br>• <b>मनसबदारी व्यवस्था</b> में अधिकारियों को <b>जात</b> (व्यक्तिगत पद) व <b>सवार</b> (घुड़सवार पद) तथा पालने वाले घुड़सवारों की संख्या से श्रेणीबद्ध किया जाता था।<br>• जहाँगीर के समय <b>दो-अस्पा-सिह-अस्पा</b> व्यवस्था में अमीर एकांतर माह में समान सवार पद हेतु दोगुने घोड़े रख सकता था।<br>• शेरशाह सूरी के राजस्व सुधार, दाग (ब्रांडिंग) प्रणाली तथा रुपया को बाद में अकबर ने अपनाकर परिष्कृत किया।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":29,"local_id":"50029","quid":"Q1000071109","section":"GK","topic":"Polity: President and Vice President of India","question":{"en":"As per Article 53 of the Indian Constitution, in whom does the executive authority of the Union formally reside? [SSC CGL 12/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"भारतीय संविधान के अनुच्छेद 53 के अनुसार, संघ की कार्यपालिका शक्ति औपचारिक रूप से किसमें निहित है? [SSC CGL 12/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Prime Minister of India","hi":"भारत के प्रधानमंत्री"},"2":{"en":"Council of Ministers","hi":"मंत्रिपरिषद"},"3":{"en":"President of India","hi":"भारत के राष्ट्रपति"},"4":{"en":"Parliament of India","hi":"भारत की संसद"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (3) – President of India</b><br><b>Article 53</b> provides that the executive power of the Union shall be vested in the <b>President</b> and shall be exercised by him directly or through officers subordinate to him in accordance with the Constitution.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• Article 53 also states that the President is the <b>Supreme Commander of the Armed Forces</b>, and the exercise of this power is regulated by law.<br>• Under <b>Article 74</b>, the President acts on the aid and advice of the Council of Ministers headed by the Prime Minister, so the real executive power lies with the Council of Ministers.<br>• The President is elected indirectly by an <b>electoral college</b> of elected members of both Houses of Parliament and of state legislative assemblies, by the system of proportional representation with a single transferable vote.<br>• The President holds office for <b>five years</b>, can be removed by impeachment for violation of the Constitution (Article 61), and the office is governed by Articles 52 to 62.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (3) – भारत के राष्ट्रपति</b><br><b>अनुच्छेद 53</b> का प्रावधान है कि संघ की कार्यपालिका शक्ति <b>राष्ट्रपति</b> में निहित होगी और उसका प्रयोग वह स्वयं अथवा अपने अधीनस्थ अधिकारियों के माध्यम से संविधान के अनुसार करेगा।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• अनुच्छेद 53 यह भी निर्धारित करता है कि राष्ट्रपति <b>सशस्त्र बलों का सर्वोच्च कमांडर</b> होता है तथा इस शक्ति का प्रयोग विधि द्वारा विनियमित होता है।<br>• <b>अनुच्छेद 74</b> के अनुसार राष्ट्रपति प्रधानमंत्री की अध्यक्षता वाली मंत्रिपरिषद की सहायता व सलाह पर कार्य करता है, अतः वास्तविक कार्यपालिका शक्ति मंत्रिपरिषद में निहित है।<br>• राष्ट्रपति का निर्वाचन अप्रत्यक्ष रूप से <b>निर्वाचक मंडल</b> द्वारा होता है, जिसमें संसद के दोनों सदनों तथा राज्य विधानसभाओं के निर्वाचित सदस्य आनुपातिक प्रतिनिधित्व व एकल संक्रमणीय मत पद्धति से भाग लेते हैं।<br>• राष्ट्रपति का कार्यकाल <b>पाँच वर्ष</b> होता है, संविधान के उल्लंघन पर महाभियोग (अनुच्छेद 61) द्वारा हटाया जा सकता है तथा यह पद अनुच्छेद 52 से 62 तक विनियमित है।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":30,"local_id":"50030","quid":"Q1000071110","section":"GK","topic":"Polity: Supreme Court and High Court","question":{"en":"Article 124 of the Constitution of India details the establishment and composition of which constitutional body? [SSC CGL 12/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"भारत के संविधान का अनुच्छेद 124 किस संवैधानिक निकाय की स्थापना एवं गठन का विवरण देता है? [SSC CGL 12/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"High Court","hi":"उच्च न्यायालय"},"2":{"en":"Supreme Court","hi":"सर्वोच्च न्यायालय"},"3":{"en":"Election Commission","hi":"निर्वाचन आयोग"},"4":{"en":"Finance Commission","hi":"वित्त आयोग"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (2) – Supreme Court</b><br><b>Article 124</b> deals with the establishment and constitution of the <b>Supreme Court of India</b> — it provides for a Chief Justice of India and such other judges as Parliament may by law determine.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• The Supreme Court was inaugurated on <b>28 January 1950</b>, and its sanctioned strength is now 34 judges (CJI plus 33).<br>• Judges are appointed by the President after consultation with the CJI and other judges, under the <b>collegium system</b> developed in the First, Second and Third Judges Cases.<br>• A Supreme Court judge retires at the age of <b>65 years</b> and can be removed only by impeachment on grounds of proved misbehaviour or incapacity under Article 124(4).<br>• The High Courts are dealt with in <b>Articles 214 to 231</b>, and judges of a High Court retire at 62; the Election Commission is covered by Article 324 and the Finance Commission by Article 280.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (2) – सर्वोच्च न्यायालय</b><br><b>अनुच्छेद 124</b> <b>भारत के सर्वोच्च न्यायालय</b> की स्थापना व गठन से संबंधित है — यह भारत के मुख्य न्यायाधीश तथा संसद द्वारा विधि से निर्धारित अन्य न्यायाधीशों का प्रावधान करता है।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• सर्वोच्च न्यायालय का उद्घाटन <b>28 जनवरी 1950</b> को हुआ तथा इसकी स्वीकृत संख्या अब 34 न्यायाधीश (मुख्य न्यायाधीश सहित 33) है।<br>• न्यायाधीशों की नियुक्ति राष्ट्रपति द्वारा मुख्य न्यायाधीश व अन्य न्यायाधीशों से परामर्श के बाद <b>कॉलेजियम व्यवस्था</b> के अंतर्गत होती है, जो प्रथम, द्वितीय व तृतीय न्यायाधीश मामलों में विकसित हुई।<br>• सर्वोच्च न्यायालय का न्यायाधीश <b>65 वर्ष</b> की आयु में सेवानिवृत्त होता है तथा अनुच्छेद 124(4) के अंतर्गत सिद्ध कदाचार या अक्षमता के आधार पर महाभियोग से ही हटाया जा सकता है।<br>• उच्च न्यायालय <b>अनुच्छेद 214 से 231</b> में आते हैं तथा उच्च न्यायालय के न्यायाधीश 62 वर्ष में सेवानिवृत्त होते हैं; निर्वाचन आयोग अनुच्छेद 324 तथा वित्त आयोग अनुच्छेद 280 के अंतर्गत है।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":31,"local_id":"50031","quid":"Q1000071111","section":"GK","topic":"Polity: Parliament","question":{"en":"Under Article 112 of the Indian Constitution, what is the official constitutional term used for the document commonly known as the \"Budget\"? [SSC CGL 12/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"भारतीय संविधान के अनुच्छेद 112 के अंतर्गत, सामान्यतः \"बजट\" कहे जाने वाले दस्तावेज़ हेतु कौन-सा आधिकारिक संवैधानिक शब्द प्रयुक्त होता है? [SSC CGL 12/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Annual Budgetary Report","hi":"वार्षिक बजटीय रिपोर्ट"},"2":{"en":"Annual Financial Statement","hi":"वार्षिक वित्तीय विवरण"},"3":{"en":"National Revenue Estimate","hi":"राष्ट्रीय राजस्व अनुमान"},"4":{"en":"Yearly Expenditure Plan","hi":"वार्षिक व्यय योजना"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (2) – Annual Financial Statement</b><br>Under <b>Article 112</b>, the document commonly called the Budget is constitutionally known as the <b>Annual Financial Statement</b> — a statement of the estimated receipts and expenditure of the Government of India for each financial year.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• The Budget is presented by the <b>Finance Minister</b> in the Lok Sabha on 1 February, and the financial year runs from 1 April to 31 March.<br>• Expenditure is of two kinds — <b>charged expenditure</b> (not voted by Parliament, such as the salary of the President and judges) and expenditure <b>made from the Consolidated Fund of India</b> (voted).<br>• The Budget is presented with the Finance Bill containing tax proposals, and <b>Article 265</b> prohibits taxation without the authority of law.<br>• Related articles are <b>Article 110</b> (Money Bill), <b>Article 112</b> (Annual Financial Statement), <b>Article 114</b> (Appropriation Bill) and <b>Article 266</b> (Consolidated and Public Accounts Funds).","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (2) – वार्षिक वित्तीय विवरण</b><br><b>अनुच्छेद 112</b> के अंतर्गत सामान्यतः बजट कहा जाने वाला दस्तावेज़ संवैधानिक रूप से <b>वार्षिक वित्तीय विवरण</b> कहलाता है — यह प्रत्येक वित्तीय वर्ष हेतु भारत सरकार की अनुमानित प्राप्तियों व व्यय का विवरण होता है।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• बजट <b>वित्त मंत्री</b> द्वारा 1 फरवरी को लोकसभा में प्रस्तुत किया जाता है तथा वित्तीय वर्ष 1 अप्रैल से 31 मार्च तक होता है।<br>• व्यय दो प्रकार का होता है — <b>भारित व्यय</b> (जिस पर संसद मतदान नहीं करती, जैसे राष्ट्रपति व न्यायाधीशों का वेतन) तथा <b>भारत की संचित निधि</b> से किया जाने वाला व्यय (मतदान के अधीन)।<br>• बजट के साथ कर प्रस्तावों वाला वित्त विधेयक प्रस्तुत होता है तथा <b>अनुच्छेद 265</b> विधि के प्राधिकार के बिना कराधान का निषेध करता है।<br>• संबंधित अनुच्छेद हैं — <b>अनुच्छेद 110</b> (धन विधेयक), <b>अनुच्छेद 112</b> (वार्षिक वित्तीय विवरण), <b>अनुच्छेद 114</b> (विनियोग विधेयक) तथा <b>अनुच्छेद 266</b> (संचित व लोक लेखा निधियाँ)।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":32,"local_id":"50032","quid":"Q1000071112","section":"GK","topic":"Modern History: Miscellaneous","question":{"en":"Under the Charter Act of 1793, for how many years was the Company’s Charter renewed? [SSC CGL 12/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"1793 के चार्टर अधिनियम के अंतर्गत कंपनी का चार्टर कितने वर्षों हेतु नवीकृत किया गया? [SSC CGL 12/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Ten years","hi":"दस वर्ष"},"2":{"en":"Fifteen years","hi":"पंद्रह वर्ष"},"3":{"en":"Twenty years","hi":"बीस वर्ष"},"4":{"en":"Thirty years","hi":"तीस वर्ष"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (3) – Twenty years</b><br>The <b>Charter Act of 1793</b> renewed the East India Company’s charter for a further <b>twenty years</b> — a practice that continued with the Charter Acts of 1813 and 1833, until the Charter Act of 1853.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• The Charter Act of 1793 extended the Company’s trade monopoly for twenty years and gave the Governor-General power to override the Council.<br>• It provided for the payment of the <b>Board of Control</b> and the salaries of the Board’s staff out of Indian revenues, and laid down that the members of the Board of Trade would be appointed by the Crown.<br>• The <b>Charter Act of 1813</b> ended the Company’s monopoly of Indian trade (except tea and China trade) and earmarked one lakh rupees for education.<br>• The <b>Charter Act of 1833</b> made the Governor-General of Bengal the <b>Governor-General of India</b> (first: Lord William Bentinck) and the <b>Charter Act of 1853</b> introduced the open competitive examination for the civil services.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (3) – बीस वर्ष</b><br><b>1793 का चार्टर अधिनियम</b> ने ईस्ट इंडिया कंपनी के चार्टर को आगामी <b>बीस वर्षों</b> हेतु नवीकृत किया — यही परंपरा 1813 व 1833 के चार्टर अधिनियमों तक चली और 1853 के चार्टर अधिनियम पर समाप्त हुई।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• 1793 के चार्टर अधिनियम ने कंपनी के व्यापारिक एकाधिकार को बीस वर्ष बढ़ाया तथा गवर्नर-जनरल को परिषद के निर्णय को अतिक्रमित करने की शक्ति दी।<br>• इसने <b>नियंत्रण बोर्ड</b> तथा बोर्ड के कर्मचारियों के वेतन का भुगतान भारतीय राजस्व से करने का प्रावधान किया तथा बोर्ड ऑफ ट्रेड के सदस्यों की नियुक्ति क्राउन द्वारा निर्धारित की।<br>• <b>1813 के चार्टर अधिनियम</b> ने भारतीय व्यापार पर कंपनी का एकाधिकार समाप्त किया (चाय व चीन व्यापार को छोड़कर) तथा शिक्षा हेतु एक लाख रुपये निर्धारित किए।<br>• <b>1833 का चार्टर अधिनियम</b> ने बंगाल के गवर्नर-जनरल को <b>भारत का गवर्नर-जनरल</b> बनाया (प्रथम: लॉर्ड विलियम बेंटिक) तथा <b>1853 के चार्टर अधिनियम</b> ने सिविल सेवा हेतु खुली प्रतियोगी परीक्षा शुरू की।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":33,"local_id":"50033","quid":"Q1000071113","section":"GK","topic":"Geography: Earth's Interior and Plate Tectonics & Latitude and Longitude","question":{"en":"What is the term used for the structural deformation of the lithosphere resulting in the formation of mountain ranges? [SSC CGL 12/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"पर्वत श्रृंखलाओं के निर्माण के परिणामस्वरूप स्थलमंडल के संरचनात्मक विरूपण हेतु कौन-सा शब्द प्रयुक्त होता है? [SSC CGL 12/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Orogeny","hi":"पर्वतजनन"},"2":{"en":"Epeirogeny","hi":"महाद्वीपजनन"},"3":{"en":"Isostasy","hi":"समस्थिति"},"4":{"en":"Tectonism","hi":"विवर्तनिकी"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (1) – Orogeny</b><br><b>Orogeny</b> is the process of mountain building through the structural deformation of the lithosphere — folding, faulting and crustal thickening — caused by the collision of tectonic plates, as in the Himalayas and the Alps.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• <b>Epeirogeny</b> refers to the broad, slow uplift or subsidence of continents without much folding, and <b>isostasy</b> is the state of gravitational balance between the lithosphere and the asthenosphere.<br>• Orogenic belts are formed at <b>convergent plate boundaries</b>, where oceanic or continental plates collide; the Himalayas arose from the collision of the Indian and Eurasian plates.<br>• Mountains formed by orogeny are of two types — <b>fold mountains</b> (Himalayas, Andes) and <b>block mountains</b> (Vosges, Black Forest).<br>• The word comes from the Greek <i>oros</i> (mountain) and <i>genesis</i> (creation), and the cycle of erosion that follows uplift was described by W.M. Davis.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (1) – पर्वतजनन</b><br><b>पर्वतजनन (Orogeny)</b> स्थलमंडल के संरचनात्मक विरूपण — वलन, भ्रंशन तथा भूपर्पटी के मोटा होने — के माध्यम से पर्वत निर्माण की प्रक्रिया है, जो विवर्तनिक प्लेटों के टकराव से होती है, जैसे हिमालय व आल्प्स में।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• <b>महाद्वीपजनन (Epeirogeny)</b> बिना अधिक वलन के महाद्वीपों के व्यापक, मंद उत्थान या अवतलन को कहते हैं, तथा <b>समस्थिति (Isostasy)</b> स्थलमंडल व दुर्बलमंडल के बीच गुरुत्वीय संतुलन की स्थिति है।<br>• पर्वतजनन पट्टियाँ <b>अभिसारी प्लेट सीमाओं</b> पर बनती हैं, जहाँ महासागरीय या महाद्वीपीय प्लेटें टकराती हैं; हिमालय भारतीय व यूरेशियाई प्लेटों के टकराव से बना।<br>• पर्वतजनन से बने पर्वत दो प्रकार के होते हैं — <b>वलन पर्वत</b> (हिमालय, एंडीज़) तथा <b>भ्रंश पर्वत</b> (वोस्गेस, ब्लैक फॉरेस्ट)।<br>• यह शब्द ग्रीक <i>ओरोस</i> (पर्वत) व <i>जेनेसिस</i> (सृष्टि) से बना है; उत्थान के बाद होने वाले अपरदन-चक्र का वर्णन डब्ल्यू.एम. डेविस ने किया।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":34,"local_id":"50034","quid":"Q1000071114","section":"GK","topic":"Static GK: Sports(Static & Current)","question":{"en":"Sprinter S. Dhanalakshmi received an eight-year ban in 2025 after testing positive for drostanolone. This sanction most likely indicates a: [SSC CGL 12/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"धाविका एस. धनलक्ष्मी को 2025 में ड्रोस्टैनोलोन के लिए पॉज़िटिव पाए जाने के बाद आठ वर्ष का प्रतिबंध मिला। यह दंड सर्वाधिक संभावित रूप से किसे दर्शाता है? [SSC CGL 12/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"First violation","hi":"प्रथम उल्लंघन"},"2":{"en":"Second violation","hi":"द्वितीय उल्लंघन"},"3":{"en":"Minor offence","hi":"मामूली अपराध"},"4":{"en":"Filing error","hi":"फाइलिंग त्रुटि"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (2) – Second violation</b><br>An <b>eight-year</b> ban indicates a <b>second anti-doping violation</b>. Under the World Anti-Doping Code a first serious violation carries a four-year suspension, which is doubled for a repeat offence; Dhanalakshmi had earlier served a ban for metandienone before testing positive for drostanolone in 2025.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• <b>S. Dhanalakshmi</b> is a Tamil Nadu sprinter who clocked 11.06 seconds in the 100 m at the National Championships and won a bronze in the 4 × 100 m relay at the 2018 Asian Games.<br>• Doping control in India is carried out by the <b>National Anti-Doping Agency (NADA)</b>, established in 2005 under the WADA framework.<br>• <b>Drostanolone</b> is an anabolic androgenic steroid used to build muscle mass and is a prohibited substance in the WADA list.<br>• Sanctions for a second violation may be up to a lifetime ban, and all medals and results from the period of the violation are annulled.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (2) – द्वितीय उल्लंघन</b><br><b>आठ वर्ष</b> का प्रतिबंध <b>दूसरे डोपिंग उल्लंघन</b> को दर्शाता है। विश्व डोप-विरोधी संहिता के अनुसार पहले गंभीर उल्लंघन पर चार वर्ष का निलंबन होता है, जो दोबारा उल्लंघन पर दोगुना हो जाता है; धनलक्ष्मी 2025 में ड्रोस्टैनोलोन हेतु पॉज़िटिव होने से पहले मेटैंडिएनोन हेतु प्रतिबंध झेल चुकी थीं।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• <b>एस. धनलक्ष्मी</b> तमिलनाडु की धाविका हैं, जिन्होंने राष्ट्रीय चैंपियनशिप में 100 मीटर में 11.06 सेकंड का समय लिया तथा 2018 एशियाई खेलों में 4 × 100 मीटर रिले में कांस्य जीता।<br>• भारत में डोपिंग नियंत्रण <b>राष्ट्रीय डोप-विरोधी एजेंसी (NADA)</b> करती है, जिसकी स्थापना 2005 में WADA ढाँचे के अंतर्गत हुई।<br>• <b>ड्रोस्टैनोलोन</b> एक एनाबॉलिक एंड्रोजेनिक स्टेरॉयड है, जिसका उपयोग मांसपेशियाँ बढ़ाने हेतु होता है और यह WADA की प्रतिबंधित सूची में है।<br>• दूसरे उल्लंघन पर आजीवन प्रतिबंध तक हो सकता है तथा उल्लंघन की अवधि के सभी पदक व परिणाम निरस्त कर दिए जाते हैं।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":35,"local_id":"50035","quid":"Q1000071115","section":"GK","topic":"Static GK: Folk Dances and Festivals","question":{"en":"The Yemshe Festival is a major traditional festival associated with which of the following tribes? [SSC CGL 12/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"येम्शे उत्सव निम्नलिखित में से किस जनजाति से संबंधित एक प्रमुख पारंपरिक उत्सव है? [SSC CGL 12/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Ao tribe","hi":"आओ जनजाति"},"2":{"en":"Angami tribe","hi":"अंगामी जनजाति"},"3":{"en":"Lotha tribe","hi":"लोथा जनजाति"},"4":{"en":"Pochuri tribe","hi":"पोचुरी जनजाति"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (4) – Pochuri tribe</b><br>The <b>Yemshe</b> festival is the major harvest festival of the <b>Pochuri (Pouchury) tribe</b> of Nagaland, celebrated in October after the sowing season, with traditional songs, dances and offerings of the first harvest.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• The Pochuri are one of the major <b>Naga tribes</b> of Nagaland, concentrated in the Phek and Tuensang districts, and Yemshe is their biggest festival.<br>• Other Naga festivals are <b>Sekrenyi</b> (Angami), <b>Moatsu</b> (Ao), <b>Tokhu Emong</b> (Lotha), <b>Aoleang</b> (Konyak) and <b>Hornbill Festival</b> (a state-level festival of all Naga tribes held in December at Kisama).<br>• Nagaland has 17 recognised tribes and the Hornbill Festival, started in 2000, is called the \"festival of festivals\".<br>• Harvest festivals of other states include Bihu (Assam), Makar Sankranti, Pongal (Tamil Nadu), Onam (Kerala) and Baisakhi (Punjab).","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (4) – पोचुरी जनजाति</b><br><b>येम्शे</b> उत्सव नागालैंड की <b>पोचुरी</b> जनजाति का प्रमुख फसल उत्सव है, जो बुवाई के मौसम के बाद अक्टूबर में पारंपरिक गीतों-नृत्यों तथा प्रथम फसल की भेंट के साथ मनाया जाता है।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• पोचुरी नागालैंड की प्रमुख <b>नागा जनजातियों</b> में से एक हैं, जो मुख्यतः फेक व तुएनसांग जिलों में निवास करते हैं, और येम्शे उनका सबसे बड़ा उत्सव है।<br>• अन्य नागा उत्सव हैं — <b>सेक्रेन्यी</b> (अंगामी), <b>मोआत्सु</b> (आओ), <b>तोखु इमोंग</b> (लोथा), <b>आओलेआंग</b> (कोन्याक) तथा <b>हॉर्नबिल उत्सव</b> (दिसंबर में किसामा में सभी नागा जनजातियों का राज्य-स्तरीय उत्सव)।<br>• नागालैंड में 17 मान्यता प्राप्त जनजातियाँ हैं तथा 2000 से आरंभ हॉर्नबिल उत्सव को \"उत्सवों का उत्सव\" कहा जाता है।<br>• अन्य राज्यों के फसल उत्सवों में बिहू (असम), मकर संक्रांति, पोंगल (तमिलनाडु), ओणम (केरल) तथा बैसाखी (पंजाब) सम्मिलित हैं।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":36,"local_id":"50036","quid":"Q1000071116","section":"GK","topic":"Static GK: Sports(Static & Current)","question":{"en":"What does a yellow card signify in football? [SSC CGL 12/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"फुटबॉल में पीला कार्ड क्या दर्शाता है? [SSC CGL 12/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"A goal is awarded","hi":"गोल दिया जाता है"},"2":{"en":"A caution to the player","hi":"खिलाड़ी को चेतावनी"},"3":{"en":"A substitution is required","hi":"खिलाड़ी परिवर्तन आवश्यक है"},"4":{"en":"The match is terminated","hi":"मैच समाप्त कर दिया जाता है"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (2) – A caution to the player</b><br>In football a <b>yellow card</b> is shown to a player as a formal <b>caution</b> for an offence such as a reckless foul, dissent, delaying the restart or unsporting behaviour. Two yellow cards in the same match result in a red card and the player’s dismissal.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• The card system was introduced at the <b>1970 FIFA World Cup</b> on the suggestion of referee Ken Aston.<br>• A <b>red card</b> means the player is sent off and the team plays with one player less; a red card for serious foul play may lead to a longer suspension.<br>• A football team has <b>11 players</b> on the field, and a match has two halves of 45 minutes each with a 15-minute interval.<br>• Football is governed internationally by <b>FIFA</b>, and the <b>FIFA World Cup</b> is held every four years; India won the SAFF Championship a record number of times.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (2) – खिलाड़ी को चेतावनी</b><br>फुटबॉल में <b>पीला कार्ड</b> खिलाड़ी को लापरवाह फाउल, रेफरी के निर्णय का विरोध, खेल आरंभ में विलंब या अखिलाड़ीय व्यवहार जैसे अपराध हेतु औपचारिक <b>चेतावनी</b> के रूप में दिखाया जाता है। एक ही मैच में दो पीले कार्ड लाल कार्ड बनकर खिलाड़ी को बाहर कर देते हैं।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• कार्ड प्रणाली <b>1970 के फीफा विश्व कप</b> में रेफरी केन एस्टन के सुझाव पर शुरू की गई।<br>• <b>लाल कार्ड</b> का अर्थ है खिलाड़ी को मैदान से बाहर करना और टीम एक खिलाड़ी कम के साथ खेलती है; गंभीर फाउल पर दीर्घ निलंबन भी हो सकता है।<br>• फुटबॉल टीम में मैदान पर <b>11 खिलाड़ी</b> होते हैं तथा मैच 45-45 मिनट के दो हाफ में खेला जाता है, बीच में 15 मिनट का विराम होता है।<br>• अंतर्राष्ट्रीय स्तर पर फुटबॉल का संचालन <b>फीफा</b> करता है और <b>फीफा विश्व कप</b> प्रत्येक चार वर्ष में होता है।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":37,"local_id":"50037","quid":"Q1000071117","section":"GK","topic":"Static GK: Folk Dances and Festivals","question":{"en":"Identify the <b>correct</b> match between the traditional folk dance and its associated state: [SSC CGL 12/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"पारंपरिक लोक नृत्य तथा उससे संबंधित राज्य के बीच <b>सही</b> मिलान पहचानिए: [SSC CGL 12/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Matki - Madhya Pradesh","hi":"मटकी - मध्य प्रदेश"},"2":{"en":"Pandavani - Uttar Pradesh","hi":"पंडवानी - उत्तर प्रदेश"},"3":{"en":"Chhau Lam - Nagaland","hi":"छाऊ लाम - नागालैंड"},"4":{"en":"Karakattam - Kerala","hi":"करगाट्टम - केरल"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (1) – Matki - Madhya Pradesh</b><br><b>Matki</b> is a popular folk dance of the <b>Malwa region of Madhya Pradesh</b>, performed by women balancing a pot (matki) on the head, often with the Maanch and Garba-style movements. The other pairs are wrong: Pandavani is from Chhattisgarh, Chhau of Seraikella is from Jharkhand (Chhau forms belong to Odisha, Jharkhand and West Bengal) and Karakattam is from Tamil Nadu.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• Famous folk dances: <b>Bihu</b> (Assam), Garba (Gujarat), Ghoomar (Rajasthan), Bhangra (Punjab), Lavani (Maharashtra), Kummi (Tamil Nadu).<br>• <b>Chhau</b> is a semi-classical dance with three styles — Seraikella (Jharkhand), Purulia (West Bengal) and Mayurbhanj (Odisha); it is on the UNESCO representative list.<br>• <b>Pandavani</b> is a traditional folk balladeer form of Chhattisgarh that narrates episodes of the Mahabharata; <b>Karakattam</b> is the Tamil \"pot dance\" performed with a decorated pot on the head.<br>• The <b>Sangeet Natak Akademi</b> confers awards for folk and traditional arts, and the Ministry of Culture documents folk dances of the states.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (1) – मटकी - मध्य प्रदेश</b><br><b>मटकी</b> <b>मध्य प्रदेश के मालवा क्षेत्र</b> का लोकप्रिय लोक नृत्य है, जिसमें महिलाएँ सिर पर मटका (घड़ा) संतुलित करके, अकसर मांच व गरबा जैसी गतियों के साथ नृत्य करती हैं। शेष युग्म गलत हैं: पंडवानी छत्तीसगढ़ की है, सरायकेला का छाऊ झारखंड का (छाऊ के रूप ओडिशा, झारखंड व पश्चिम बंगाल में) तथा करगाट्टम तमिलनाडु का है।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• प्रसिद्ध लोक नृत्य: <b>बिहू</b> (असम), गरबा (गुजरात), घूमर (राजस्थान), भांगड़ा (पंजाब), लावणी (महाराष्ट्र), कुम्मी (तमिलनाडु)।<br>• <b>छाऊ</b> अर्ध-शास्त्रीय नृत्य है जिसकी तीन शैलियाँ हैं — सरायकेला (झारखंड), पुरुलिया (पश्चिम बंगाल) तथा मयूरभंज (ओडिशा); यह यूनेस्को की प्रतिनिधि सूची में सम्मिलित है।<br>• <b>पंडवानी</b> छत्तीसगढ़ की पारंपरिक लोक-गाथा शैली है जिसमें महाभारत की कथाएँ गाई जाती हैं; <b>करगाट्टम</b> तमिलनाडु का \"घट नृत्य\" है, जिसमें सजे घड़े को सिर पर रखकर नृत्य होता है।<br>• <b>संगीत नाटक अकादमी</b> लोक व पारंपरिक कलाओं हेतु पुरस्कार देती है तथा संस्कृति मंत्रालय राज्यों के लोक नृत्यों का प्रलेखन करता है।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":38,"local_id":"50038","quid":"Q1000071118","section":"GK","topic":"Static GK: Music and Musical Instruments","question":{"en":"Which of the following traditional folk songs is native to Haryana? [SSC CGL 12/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"निम्नलिखित में से कौन-सा पारंपरिक लोकगीत हरियाणा का मूल है? [SSC CGL 12/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Jakari","hi":"जाकड़ी"},"2":{"en":"Povada","hi":"पोवाड़ा"},"3":{"en":"Lavani","hi":"लावणी"},"4":{"en":"Garba","hi":"गरबा"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (1) – Jakari</b><br><b>Jakari</b> is a popular traditional folk song of <b>Haryana</b>, sung by women while working in the fields and during festivals. Povada and Lavani belong to Maharashtra and Garba to Gujarat.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• Other folk songs of Haryana are <b>Ragani, Saang, Chaupaiya and Bhajan</b>, and the state’s folk dances include the Phag, Saang and Dhamal.<br>• <b>Povada</b> is a Marathi ballad form that narrates the heroic deeds of Chhatrapati Shivaji Maharaj and is written in verse.<br>• <b>Lavani</b> is the most popular folk dance-song of Maharashtra, performed to the beats of the dholki; <b>Garba</b> is the Gujarati dance performed during Navratri around the garbo.<br>• Haryana’s folk theatre <b>Saang</b> and the Ragini style of singing are popular in the Rohtak–Sonipat belt, and Deep Chand Bahman is a noted Saang exponent.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (1) – जाकड़ी</b><br><b>जाकड़ी</b> <b>हरियाणा</b> का लोकप्रिय पारंपरिक लोकगीत है, जिसे महिलाएँ खेतों में काम करते समय तथा त्योहारों पर गाती हैं। पोवाड़ा व लावणी महाराष्ट्र के तथा गरबा गुजरात का लोकगीत-नृत्य है।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• हरियाणा के अन्य लोकगीत <b>रागिनी, सांग, चौपइया व भजन</b> हैं, तथा राज्य के लोक नृत्यों में फाग, सांग व धमाल सम्मिलित हैं।<br>• <b>पोवाड़ा</b> मराठी गाथा शैली है, जिसमें छत्रपति शिवाजी महाराज के वीर कार्यों का पद्य रूप में वर्णन होता है।<br>• <b>लावणी</b> महाराष्ट्र का सर्वाधिक लोकप्रिय लोक नृत्य-गीत है, जो ढोलकी की ताल पर होता है; <b>गरबा</b> गुजरात का नृत्य है, जो नवरात्रि में गरबे के चारों ओर किया जाता है।<br>• हरियाणा का लोक रंगमंच <b>सांग</b> तथा रागिनी गायन शैली रोहतक–सोनीपत क्षेत्र में लोकप्रिय है; दीपचंद बहमन सांग के प्रसिद्ध कलाकार हैं।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":39,"local_id":"50039","quid":"Q1000071119","section":"GK","topic":"Current Affairs: Government Schemes and Policies (Current)","question":{"en":"Which technology is primarily used for mapping rural inhabited lands under the SVAMITVA scheme? is designed to enhance the capacity and skills of which group in India? [SSC CGL 12/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"स्वामित्व योजना के अंतर्गत ग्रामीण आबादी वाली भूमियों के मानचित्रण हेतु मुख्यतः कौन-सी तकनीक प्रयुक्त होती है? भारत में यह किस समूह की क्षमता व कौशल बढ़ाने हेतु है? [SSC CGL 12/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"School students in rural areas","hi":"ग्रामीण क्षेत्रों के स्कूली विद्यार्थी"},"2":{"en":"Civil Servants in India","hi":"भारत के सिविल सेवक"},"3":{"en":"Unorganized sector workers","hi":"असंगठित क्षेत्र के श्रमिक"},"4":{"en":"Small and Medium Entrepreneurs","hi":"लघु एवं मध्यम उद्यमी"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (2) – Civil Servants in India</b><br>The <b>SVAMITVA scheme</b> uses <b>drone-based survey technology</b> to map rural inhabited land parcels and issue property cards to owners, while the capacity-building of government servants is the aim of <b>Mission Karmayogi</b> — the National Programme for Civil Services Capacity Building. Hence the group indicated here is <b>Civil Servants in India</b>.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• SVAMITVA (Survey of Villages and Mapping with Improvised Technology in Village Areas) was launched on <b>24 April 2020</b> by the Ministry of Panchayati Raj.<br>• It issues <b>property cards (Adhikar Abhilekh)</b> to rural households, enabling them to use property as collateral for loans and reducing property disputes.<br>• The scheme uses <b>drone survey and CORS technology</b> and covers about 6.62 lakh villages; it is implemented with the Survey of India and NIC.<br>• <b>Mission Karmayogi</b> (2020) is implemented through the Capacity Building Commission and aims to shift civil servants from \"rule-based\" to \"role-based\" competency.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (2) – भारत के सिविल सेवक</b><br><b>स्वामित्व योजना</b> ग्रामीण आबादी वाली भूमि खंडों का मानचित्रण करने तथा स्वामियों को संपत्ति कार्ड जारी करने हेतु <b>ड्रोन-आधारित सर्वेक्षण तकनीक</b> का उपयोग करती है, जबकि सरकारी कर्मचारियों की क्षमता-निर्माण <b>मिशन कर्मयोगी</b> — सिविल सेवा क्षमता निर्माण हेतु राष्ट्रीय कार्यक्रम — का लक्ष्य है। अतः यहाँ संकेतित समूह <b>भारत के सिविल सेवक</b> हैं।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• स्वामित्व योजना (Survey of Villages and Mapping with Improvised Technology in Village Areas) का शुभारंभ <b>24 अप्रैल 2020</b> को पंचायती राज मंत्रालय द्वारा हुआ।<br>• यह ग्रामीण परिवारों को <b>संपत्ति कार्ड (अधिकार अभिलेख)</b> जारी करती है, जिससे वे संपत्ति को ऋण हेतु प्रतिभूति बना सकते हैं और संपत्ति विवाद घटते हैं।<br>• योजना <b>ड्रोन सर्वेक्षण व CORS तकनीक</b> का उपयोग करती है और लगभग 6.62 लाख गाँवों को समाहित करती है; इसे भारतीय सर्वेक्षण व NIC के साथ क्रियान्वित किया जाता है।<br>• <b>मिशन कर्मयोगी</b> (2020) क्षमता निर्माण आयोग के माध्यम से क्रियान्वित होता है और सिविल सेवकों को \"नियम-आधारित\" से \"भूमिका-आधारित\" दक्षता की ओर ले जाना चाहता है।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":40,"local_id":"50040","quid":"Q1000071120","section":"GK","topic":"Static GK: Awards and Honours","question":{"en":"Which of the following Urdu books and their author won the Bal Sahitya Puraskar 2025? [SSC CGL 12/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"निम्नलिखित में से कौन-सी उर्दू पुस्तक तथा उसके लेखक ने बाल साहित्य पुरस्कार 2025 जीता? [SSC CGL 12/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Auraq-e-Science by Abdul Ansari","hi":"औराक-ए-साइंस - अब्दुल अंसारी"},"2":{"en":"Qaumi Sitare by Ghazanfar Iqbal","hi":"कौमी सितारे - ग़ज़नफ़र इक़बाल"},"3":{"en":"Abba Jaan by Raunaq Jamal","hi":"अब्बा जान - रौनक जमाल"},"4":{"en":"Ummeedun Ke Phool by Habib Saifi","hi":"उम्मीदों के फूल - हबीब सैफी"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (2) – Qaumi Sitare by Ghazanfar Iqbal</b><br>The Sahitya Akademi’s <b>Bal Sahitya Puraskar 2025</b> for Urdu was awarded to <b>Ghazanfar Iqbal</b> for his book <b><i>Qaumi Sitare</i></b>, a collection of articles written for children.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• The Bal Sahitya Puraskar was announced for <b>24 Indian languages</b> and presented on 14 November 2025, on the eve of Children’s Day, at the Triveni Auditorium, New Delhi.<br>• Each awardee receives a cheque of <b>₹50,000</b> and a bronze plaque; the award was instituted in 2010.<br>• The Sahitya Akademi, established in <b>1954</b>, is the national academy of letters and awards the Sahitya Akademi Award and the Yuva Puraskar as well.<br>• Other 2025 Bal Sahitya Puraskar winners include Vishnupuram Sarvanan (Tamil), Gangisetty Sivakumar (Telugu) and Heena Agnani (Sindhi).","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (2) – कौमी सितारे - ग़ज़नफ़र इक़बाल</b><br>साहित्य अकादमी का <b>बाल साहित्य पुरस्कार 2025</b> उर्दू हेतु <b>ग़ज़नफ़र इक़बाल</b> को उनकी पुस्तक <b><i>कौमी सितारे</i></b> — बच्चों हेतु लिखे गए लेखों के संग्रह — के लिए दिया गया।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• बाल साहित्य पुरस्कार <b>24 भारतीय भाषाओं</b> हेतु घोषित किया गया तथा 14 नवंबर 2025 को बाल दिवस की पूर्व संध्या पर नई दिल्ली के त्रिवेणी सभागार में प्रदान किया गया।<br>• प्रत्येक विजेता को <b>₹50,000</b> का चेक तथा कांस्य फलक मिलता है; यह पुरस्कार 2010 में आरंभ हुआ।<br>• <b>1954</b> में स्थापित साहित्य अकादमी देश की राष्ट्रीय साहित्य संस्था है, जो साहित्य अकादमी पुरस्कार तथा युवा पुरस्कार भी देती है।<br>• 2025 के अन्य बाल साहित्य पुरस्कार विजेताओं में विष्णुपुरम सर्वानन (तमिल), गंगिसेट्टी शिवकुमार (तेलुगु) तथा हीना अगनानी (सिंधी) सम्मिलित हैं।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":41,"local_id":"50041","quid":"Q1000071121","section":"GK","topic":"Current Affairs: International News","question":{"en":"Which concept is most closely associated with the strategic vision of the Quadrilateral Security Dialogue (QUAD)? [SSC CGL 12/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"क्वाड (चतुष्पक्षीय सुरक्षा संवाद) की रणनीतिक दृष्टि से कौन-सी अवधारणा सर्वाधिक निकटता से जुड़ी है? [SSC CGL 12/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Free and Open Indo-Pacific","hi":"स्वतंत्र और खुला हिंद-प्रशांत"},"2":{"en":"Continental Security and Land Bloc","hi":"महाद्वीपीय सुरक्षा और भूमि गुट"},"3":{"en":"Atlantic Partnership and North Atlantic Treaty Organization (NATO) Framework","hi":"अटलांटिक साझेदारी और उत्तरी अटलांटिक संधि संगठन (NATO) ढाँचा"},"4":{"en":"Eurasian Integration and Continental Order","hi":"यूरेशियाई एकीकरण और महाद्वीपीय व्यवस्था"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (1) – Free and Open Indo-Pacific</b><br>The Quad, comprising <b>India, the United States, Japan and Australia</b>, is built around the vision of a <b>free, open, inclusive and rules-based Indo-Pacific</b> — a concept that rejects coercion in the maritime domain and upholds freedom of navigation.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• The Quad began as a dialogue after the <b>2004 Indian Ocean tsunami</b> and was upgraded to leader-level summits from 2021; India hosted the Quad Summit in 2021.<br>• Its working groups cover vaccines, critical and emerging technologies, climate action, maritime security and infrastructure.<br>• The Quad’s initiatives include the <b>Indo-Pacific Maritime Domain Awareness (IPMDA)</b> initiative, the Quad Vaccine Partnership and the Quad Fellowship.<br>• The Quad is not a military alliance and has no treaty obligations; it works alongside groupings such as <b>ASEAN, I2U2 and the Indian Ocean Rim Association</b>.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (1) – स्वतंत्र और खुला हिंद-प्रशांत</b><br>क्वाड — <b>भारत, संयुक्त राज्य अमेरिका, जापान व ऑस्ट्रेलिया</b> — <b>स्वतंत्र, खुले, समावेशी व नियम-आधारित हिंद-प्रशांत</b> की दृष्टि पर आधारित है, जो समुद्री क्षेत्र में दबाव की नीति का विरोध तथा नौवहन स्वतंत्रता का समर्थन करती है।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• क्वाड का आरंभ <b>2004 की हिंद महासागर सुनामी</b> के बाद संवाद के रूप में हुआ और 2021 से इसे नेताओं के शिखर सम्मेलन का दर्जा मिला; 2021 में भारत ने क्वाड शिखर सम्मेलन की मेज़बानी की।<br>• इसके कार्यकारी समूह टीके, उभरती हुई प्रौद्योगिकियाँ, जलवायु कार्रवाई, समुद्री सुरक्षा तथा अवसंरचना पर काम करते हैं।<br>• क्वाड की पहलों में <b>हिंद-प्रशांत समुद्री क्षेत्र जागरूकता (IPMDA)</b>, क्वाड वैक्सीन साझेदारी तथा क्वाड फेलोशिप सम्मिलित हैं।<br>• क्वाड सैन्य गठबंधन नहीं है और इस पर कोई संधि-बाध्यता नहीं है; यह <b>आसियान, I2U2 तथा हिंद महासागर रिम संघ</b> जैसे समूहों के साथ कार्य करता है।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":42,"local_id":"50042","quid":"Q1000071122","section":"GK","topic":"Polity: New Criminal Laws 2023","question":{"en":"In a murder trial, A claims that at the time of the act he was incapable of understanding the nature of his conduct due to unsoundness of mind. Which category does this circumstance primarily fall under the Bharatiya Nyaya Sanhita, 2023 in India? [SSC CGL 12/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"एक हत्या के मुकदमे में A दावा करता है कि कार्य के समय मानसिक अस्वस्थता के कारण वह अपने आचरण की प्रकृति समझने में असमर्थ था। भारत में भारतीय न्याय संहिता, 2023 के अंतर्गत यह परिस्थिति मुख्यतः किस श्रेणी में आती है? [SSC CGL 12/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Relevant fact only","hi":"केवल सुसंगत तथ्य"},"2":{"en":"Fact in issue","hi":"विवाद्य तथ्य"},"3":{"en":"Documentary evidence","hi":"प्रलेखी साक्ष्य"},"4":{"en":"Conclusive proof","hi":"निर्णायक प्रमाण"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (2) – Fact in issue</b><br>Whether the accused was of unsound mind at the time of the act is a <b>fact in issue</b> in the trial, because it directly determines criminal liability. Section 22 of the Bharatiya Nyaya Sanhita, 2023 (the old Section 84 of the IPC) gives the defence of unsoundness of mind.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• <b>Section 22 BNS</b> states that nothing is an offence which is done by a person who, at the time of doing it, by reason of unsoundness of mind, is incapable of knowing the nature of the act or that it is wrong or contrary to law.<br>• The burden of proving insanity in India lies on the <b>accused</b>, who must show it by the standard of the \"prudent man\" — the <b>McNaughton Rules</b> form the basis of this defence.<br>• The three new criminal laws — <b>Bharatiya Nyaya Sanhita, Bharatiya Nagarik Suraksha Sanhita and Bharatiya Sakshya Adhiniyam</b> — replaced the IPC, CrPC and Indian Evidence Act from 1 July 2024.<br>• <b>Fact in issue</b> is defined in the Bharatiya Sakshya Adhiniyam as a fact from which the existence or non-existence of a right or liability can be inferred.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (2) – विवाद्य तथ्य</b><br>क्या अभियुक्त कार्य के समय मानसिक रूप से अस्वस्थ था — यह मुकदमे में <b>विवाद्य तथ्य</b> है, क्योंकि इससे दंडात्मक दायित्व सीधे निर्धारित होता है। भारतीय न्याय संहिता, 2023 की धारा 22 (पूर्व IPC की धारा 84) मानसिक अस्वस्थता का प्रतिरक्षा प्रदान करती है।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• <b>BNS की धारा 22</b> के अनुसार उस व्यक्ति द्वारा किया गया कार्य अपराध नहीं है, जो कार्य के समय मानसिक अस्वस्थता के कारण उसकी प्रकृति अथवा उसके अनुचित या विधि-विरुद्ध होने को जानने में असमर्थ था।<br>• भारत में पागलपन सिद्ध करने का भार <b>अभियुक्त</b> पर होता है, जिसे \"विवेकशील व्यक्ति\" के मानक पर सिद्ध करना होता है; <b>मैकनॉटन नियम</b> इस प्रतिरक्षा का आधार हैं।<br>• तीन नए आपराधिक कानून — <b>भारतीय न्याय संहिता, भारतीय नागरिक सुरक्षा संहिता तथा भारतीय साक्ष्य अधिनियम</b> — ने 1 जुलाई 2024 से IPC, CrPC व भारतीय साक्ष्य अधिनियम का स्थान लिया।<br>• <b>विवाद्य तथ्य</b> को भारतीय साक्ष्य अधिनियम में ऐसे तथ्य के रूप में परिभाषित किया गया है, जिससे किसी अधिकार या दायित्व के अस्तित्व या अभाव का अनुमान लगाया जा सके।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":43,"local_id":"50043","quid":"Q1000071123","section":"GK","topic":"Static GK: Books and Authors","question":{"en":"Deepa Bhasthi translated the 2025 International Booker Prize-winning book <i>Heart Lamp</i> into English from which language? [SSC CGL 12/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"दीपा भास्थी ने 2025 का अंतर्राष्ट्रीय बुकर पुरस्कार जीतने वाली पुस्तक <i>हार्ट लैंप</i> का अंग्रेज़ी में अनुवाद किस भाषा से किया? [SSC CGL 12/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Malayalam","hi":"मलयालम"},"2":{"en":"Kannada","hi":"कन्नड़"},"3":{"en":"Tamil","hi":"तमिल"},"4":{"en":"Odia","hi":"ओड़िया"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (2) – Kannada</b><br><i>Heart Lamp</i>, the 2025 International Booker Prize-winning work of <b>Banu Mushtaq</b>, was translated from <b>Kannada</b> into English by <b>Deepa Bhasthi</b>. The award was shared by the author and the translator, who received £50,000 between them.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• <i>Heart Lamp</i> is a collection of twelve short stories selected from three decades of Banu Mushtaq’s writing, and it was the <b>first Kannada work</b> to win the International Booker.<br>• The International Booker Prize is awarded every year for a work translated into English and published in the UK or Ireland; the author and translator share the prize.<br>• Banu Mushtaq is a Kannada writer, lawyer and activist known for her short stories on the lives of Muslim women.<br>• Indian works that have won the international award include <i>Tomb of Sand</i> by Geetanjali Shree, translated by Daisy Rockwell, in 2022.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (2) – कन्नड़</b><br><b>बानू मुश्ताक</b> की 2025 के अंतर्राष्ट्रीय बुकर पुरस्कार विजेता कृति <i>हार्ट लैंप</i> का अनुवाद <b>कन्नड़</b> से अंग्रेज़ी में <b>दीपा भास्थी</b> ने किया। यह पुरस्कार लेखिका तथा अनुवादक को संयुक्त रूप से दिया गया, जिन्हें कुल £50,000 मिले।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• <i>हार्ट लैंप</i> बानू मुश्ताक के तीन दशकों के लेखन में से चुनी गई बारह कहानियों का संग्रह है और अंतर्राष्ट्रीय बुकर जीतने वाली <b>पहली कन्नड़ कृति</b> है।<br>• अंतर्राष्ट्रीय बुकर पुरस्कार प्रतिवर्ष अंग्रेज़ी में अनूदित तथा ब्रिटेन या आयरलैंड में प्रकाशित कृति हेतु दिया जाता है; पुरस्कार लेखक व अनुवादक में साझा होता है।<br>• बानू मुश्ताक कन्नड़ की लेखिका, अधिवक्ता व कार्यकर्ता हैं, जो मुस्लिम महिलाओं के जीवन पर आधारित कहानियों हेतु जानी जाती हैं।<br>• अंतर्राष्ट्रीय बुकर जीतने वाली भारतीय कृतियों में गीतांजलि श्री की <i>टॉम्ब ऑफ सैंड</i> (डेज़ी रॉकवेल द्वारा अनूदित, 2022) सम्मिलित है।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":44,"local_id":"50044","quid":"Q1000071124","section":"GK","topic":"Static GK: Census","question":{"en":"As per Census 2011, which of the following Union Territory/State–percentage pair is <b>correctly</b> matched with respect to the lowest combined Total Workforce Participation Rate (WPR)? [SSC CGL 12/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"जनगणना 2011 के अनुसार, न्यूनतम संयुक्त कुल कार्यबल भागीदारी दर (WPR) के संदर्भ में निम्नलिखित में से कौन-सा केंद्रशासित प्रदेश/राज्य–प्रतिशत युग्म <b>सही</b> सुमेलित है? [SSC CGL 12/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Lakshadweep – 29.09%","hi":"लक्षद्वीप – 29.09%"},"2":{"en":"Delhi – 27.09%","hi":"दिल्ली – 27.09%"},"3":{"en":"Bihar – 31.12%","hi":"बिहार – 31.12%"},"4":{"en":"Kerala – 32.94%","hi":"केरल – 32.94%"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (1) – Lakshadweep – 29.09%</b><br>As per Census 2011, <b>Lakshadweep had the lowest total work participation rate at 29.09%</b>. Delhi (about 33.3%), Bihar (about 34%) and Kerala (about 34.6%) had higher rates, so their figures in the options are wrong.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• The <b>work participation rate</b> is the percentage of total workers (main plus marginal) to the total population; the all-India figure in 2011 was about 39.8%.<br>• The highest work participation rate in 2011 was in <b>Himachal Pradesh (about 51.9%)</b>, followed by Nagaland and Sikkim.<br>• Census 2011 was the <b>15th census</b> and the 7th after independence; its motto was \"Our Census, Our Future\", and the population was 121.09 crore.<br>• The 2011 census recorded a <b>literacy rate of 74.04%</b>, a sex ratio of 943 and a decadal growth rate of 17.7%; Census 2027 will be India’s first digital census.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (1) – लक्षद्वीप – 29.09%</b><br>जनगणना 2011 के अनुसार <b>लक्षद्वीप में कुल कार्य भागीदारी दर सबसे कम 29.09%</b> थी। दिल्ली (लगभग 33.3%), बिहार (लगभग 34%) तथा केरल (लगभग 34.6%) की दरें अधिक थीं, अतः विकल्पों में दिए उनके आँकड़े गलत हैं।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• <b>कार्य भागीदारी दर</b> कुल कार्यकर्ताओं (मुख्य एवं सीमांत) का कुल जनसंख्या से प्रतिशत है; 2011 में अखिल भारतीय आँकड़ा लगभग 39.8% था।<br>• 2011 में सर्वाधिक कार्य भागीदारी दर <b>हिमाचल प्रदेश (लगभग 51.9%)</b> में थी, उसके बाद नागालैंड व सिक्किम।<br>• जनगणना 2011 <b>15वीं जनगणना</b> तथा स्वतंत्रता के बाद 7वीं थी; इसका आदर्श वाक्य \"हमारी जनगणना, हमारा भविष्य\" था और जनसंख्या 121.09 करोड़ रही।<br>• 2011 की जनगणना में <b>साक्षरता दर 74.04%</b>, लिंगानुपात 943 तथा दशकीय वृद्धि दर 17.7% दर्ज हुई; जनगणना 2027 भारत की पहली डिजिटल जनगणना होगी।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":45,"local_id":"50045","quid":"Q1000071125","section":"GK","topic":"Science and Technology: Science and Technology","question":{"en":"Which of the following <b>correctly</b> describes the radar payload carried by the NISAR satellite? [SSC CGL 12/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"निम्नलिखित में से कौन-सा विकल्प NISAR उपग्रह द्वारा वहन किए गए रडार पेलोड का <b>सही</b> वर्णन करता है? [SSC CGL 12/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"L-band Radar by the National Aeronautics and Space Administration and S-band Radar by the Indian Space Research Organisation","hi":"राष्ट्रीय वैमानिकी एवं अंतरिक्ष प्रशासन द्वारा L-बैंड रडार तथा भारतीय अंतरिक्ष अनुसंधान संगठन द्वारा S-बैंड रडार"},"2":{"en":"L-band Radar by the Indian Space Research Organisation and S-band Radar by the National Aeronautics and Space Administration","hi":"भारतीय अंतरिक्ष अनुसंधान संगठन द्वारा L-बैंड रडार तथा राष्ट्रीय वैमानिकी एवं अंतरिक्ष प्रशासन द्वारा S-बैंड रडार"},"3":{"en":"L-band Radar by the National Aeronautics and Space Administration and S-band Radar by the Japan Aerospace Exploration Agency","hi":"राष्ट्रीय वैमानिकी एवं अंतरिक्ष प्रशासन द्वारा L-बैंड रडार तथा जापान एयरोस्पेस एक्सप्लोरेशन एजेंसी द्वारा S-बैंड रडार"},"4":{"en":"L-band Radar by the Japan Aerospace Exploration Agency and S-band Radar by the Indian Space Research Organisation","hi":"जापान एयरोस्पेस एक्सप्लोरेशन एजेंसी द्वारा L-बैंड रडार तथा भारतीय अंतरिक्ष अनुसंधान संगठन द्वारा S-बैंड रडार"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (1) – L-band Radar by the National Aeronautics and Space Administration and S-band Radar by the Indian Space Research Organisation</b><br><b>NISAR</b> (NASA–ISRO Synthetic Aperture Radar) carries an <b>L-band radar built by NASA</b> and an <b>S-band radar built by ISRO</b>. The two frequencies together give the mission its unique ability to image the Earth’s surface through clouds, day and night.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• NISAR was launched on <b>30 July 2025</b> on ISRO’s GSLV-F16 from Sriharikota and is the most expensive Earth-imaging satellite ever built.<br>• It will observe <b>ice sheets, glaciers, sea ice, forests, wetlands and land subsidence</b> and help in earthquake and landslide studies.<br>• The L-band penetrates vegetation and the S-band is sensitive to soil moisture and biomass, making the combined data useful for agriculture and disaster management.<br>• NISAR is the first NASA–ISRO joint mission with a large hardware contribution from both agencies, and the satellite has a <b>12-day repeat cycle</b>.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (1) – राष्ट्रीय वैमानिकी एवं अंतरिक्ष प्रशासन द्वारा L-बैंड रडार तथा भारतीय अंतरिक्ष अनुसंधान संगठन द्वारा S-बैंड रडार</b><br><b>निसार</b> (NASA–ISRO सिंथेटिक एपर्चर रडार) में <b>NASA द्वारा निर्मित L-बैंड रडार</b> तथा <b>ISRO द्वारा निर्मित S-बैंड रडार</b> लगे हैं। दोनों आवृत्तियाँ मिलकर मिशन को बादलों के आर-पार दिन-रात पृथ्वी की सतह की इमेजिंग की अनूठी क्षमता देती हैं।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• निसार को <b>30 जुलाई 2025</b> को श्रीहरिकोटा से ISRO के GSLV-F16 द्वारा प्रक्षेपित किया गया; यह अब तक का सर्वाधिक खर्चीला पृथ्वी-इमेजिंग उपग्रह है।<br>• यह <b>हिमचादरों, हिमनदों, समुद्री बर्फ, वनों, आर्द्रभूमियों व भूमि धँसाव</b> का अवलोकन करेगा और भूकंप व भूस्खलन अध्ययन में सहायक होगा।<br>• L-बैंड वनस्पति में प्रवेश करता है तथा S-बैंड मृदा आर्द्रता व जैवमात्रा के प्रति संवेदनशील है, जिससे संयुक्त आँकड़े कृषि व आपदा प्रबंधन हेतु उपयोगी होते हैं।<br>• निसार NASA–ISRO का पहला संयुक्त मिशन है जिसमें दोनों एजेंसियों का बड़ा हार्डवेयर योगदान है; उपग्रह का <b>12-दिवसीय पुनरावृत्ति चक्र</b> है।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":46,"local_id":"50046","quid":"Q1000071126","section":"GK","topic":"Economics: Banking","question":{"en":"The banking sector reforms introduced after the 1991 economic reforms were implemented under the regulatory oversight of: [SSC CGL 12/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"1991 के आर्थिक सुधारों के बाद लाए गए बैंकिंग क्षेत्र के सुधार किसके नियामक पर्यवेक्षण में क्रियान्वित किए गए? [SSC CGL 12/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Insurance Regulatory Development Authority of India","hi":"भारतीय बीमा विनियामक एवं विकास प्राधिकरण"},"2":{"en":"Reserve Bank of India","hi":"भारतीय रिज़र्व बैंक"},"3":{"en":"National Bank for Agriculture and Rural Development","hi":"राष्ट्रीय कृषि और ग्रामीण विकास बैंक"},"4":{"en":"State Bank of India","hi":"भारतीय स्टेट बैंक"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (2) – Reserve Bank of India</b><br>The banking sector reforms that followed the 1991 economic reforms — prudential norms, capital adequacy, income recognition and asset classification — were implemented under the regulatory oversight of the <b>Reserve Bank of India</b>, acting on the recommendations of the Narasimham Committee.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• The <b>Narasimham Committee I (1991)</b> recommended a reduction in SLR and CRR, prudential norms and a four-tier banking structure; <b>Narasimham Committee II (1998)</b> dealt with mergers and non-performing assets.<br>• The RBI was established on <b>1 April 1935</b> under the RBI Act, 1934, and nationalised in 1949; it regulates banks, money supply and foreign exchange.<br>• Banking regulation is now shared with the <b>Banking Regulation (Amendment) Act, 2017</b>, which allowed the government to authorise the RBI on stressed assets and gave the RBI power to remove bank directors.<br>• <b>IRDAI</b> regulates insurance, <b>NABARD</b> handles rural credit and <b>SBI</b> is the country’s largest public sector bank — none of them is the banking regulator.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (2) – भारतीय रिज़र्व बैंक</b><br>1991 के आर्थिक सुधारों के बाद अपनाए गए बैंकिंग क्षेत्र के सुधार — विवेकपूर्ण मानदंड, पूँजी पर्याप्तता, आय की पहचान व परिसंपत्ति वर्गीकरण — <b>भारतीय रिज़र्व बैंक</b> के नियामक पर्यवेक्षण में नरसिंहम समिति की सिफारिशों पर क्रियान्वित किए गए।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• <b>नरसिंहम समिति I (1991)</b> ने SLR व CRR में कमी, विवेकपूर्ण मानदंड तथा चार-स्तरीय बैंकिंग संरचना की सिफारिश की; <b>नरसिंहम समिति II (1998)</b> ने विलय व गैर-निष्पादित परिसंपत्तियों पर कार्य किया।<br>• RBI की स्थापना <b>1 अप्रैल 1935</b> को RBI अधिनियम, 1934 के अंतर्गत हुई तथा 1949 में इसका राष्ट्रीयकरण हुआ; यह बैंकों, मुद्रा आपूर्ति व विदेशी मुद्रा का नियामक है।<br>• बैंकिंग नियमन अब <b>बैंकिंग विनियमन (संशोधन) अधिनियम, 2017</b> के साथ साझा है, जिसने सरकार को तनावग्रस्त परिसंपत्तियों पर RBI को अधिकृत करने और RBI को बैंक निदेशकों को हटाने की शक्ति दी।<br>• <b>IRDAI</b> बीमा का नियामक है, <b>NABARD</b> ग्रामीण ऋण देखता है तथा <b>SBI</b> देश का सबसे बड़ा सार्वजनिक क्षेत्र का बैंक है — इनमें से कोई बैंकिंग नियामक नहीं है।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":47,"local_id":"50047","quid":"Q1000071127","section":"GK","topic":"Environment: Basics of Environmental Sciences","question":{"en":"What is the primary purpose of the Air Quality Index (AQI)? [SSC CGL 12/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"वायु गुणवत्ता सूचकांक (AQI) का प्राथमिक उद्देश्य क्या है? [SSC CGL 12/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Communicate earthquake predictions in simplified form","hi":"भूकंप पूर्वानुमान को सरल रूप में प्रसारित करना"},"2":{"en":"Communicate soil fertility status in simplified form","hi":"मृदा उर्वरता की स्थिति को सरल रूप में प्रसारित करना"},"3":{"en":"Communicate water contamination status in simplified form","hi":"जल प्रदूषण की स्थिति को सरल रूप में प्रसारित करना"},"4":{"en":"Communicate air quality status in simplified form","hi":"वायु गुणवत्ता की स्थिति को सरल रूप में प्रसारित करना"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (4) – Communicate air quality status in simplified form</b><br>The Air Quality Index converts the concentrations of eight pollutants into a single number and colour code so that the <b>air quality status can be communicated to the public in a simplified form</b> — from \"Good\" to \"Severe\".<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• India’s AQI was launched by the <b>Central Pollution Control Board</b> in 2015 under the Swachh Bharat Mission, with the National Air Quality Index.<br>• The eight pollutants are <b>PM10, PM2.5, NO2, SO2, CO, O3, NH3 and Pb</b>; the index has six categories — Good (0–50), Satisfactory (51–100), Moderate (101–200), Poor (201–300), Very Poor (301–400) and Severe (401–500).<br>• AQI is monitored through the <b>National Air Quality Monitoring Programme (NAMP)</b>, which now has over 900 monitoring stations.<br>• The <b>Graded Response Action Plan (GRAP)</b> for Delhi–NCR uses AQI levels to trigger restrictions on construction, traffic and industrial activity.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (4) – वायु गुणवत्ता की स्थिति को सरल रूप में प्रसारित करना</b><br>वायु गुणवत्ता सूचकांक आठ प्रदूषकों की सांद्रता को एक संख्या व रंग-कोड में बदल देता है, जिससे <b>वायु गुणवत्ता की स्थिति जनता तक सरल रूप में प्रसारित</b> हो सके — \"अच्छा\" से \"गंभीर\" तक।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• भारत का AQI <b>केंद्रीय प्रदूषण नियंत्रण बोर्ड</b> ने 2015 में स्वच्छ भारत मिशन के अंतर्गत राष्ट्रीय वायु गुणवत्ता सूचकांक के रूप में शुरू किया।<br>• आठ प्रदूषक <b>PM10, PM2.5, NO2, SO2, CO, O3, NH3 तथा Pb</b> हैं; सूचकांक की छह श्रेणियाँ हैं — अच्छा (0–50), संतोषजनक (51–100), मध्यम (101–200), खराब (201–300), बहुत खराब (301–400) व गंभीर (401–500)।<br>• AQI का अनुश्रवण <b>राष्ट्रीय वायु गुणवत्ता अनुश्रवण कार्यक्रम (NAMP)</b> से होता है, जिसमें अब 900 से अधिक केंद्र हैं।<br>• दिल्ली–NCR हेतु <b>श्रेणीबद्ध प्रत्युत्तर कार्रवाई योजना (GRAP)</b> AQI स्तरों के आधार पर निर्माण, यातायात व औद्योगिक गतिविधि पर प्रतिबंध लगाती है।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":48,"local_id":"50048","quid":"Q1000071128","section":"GK","topic":"Medieval History: Miscellaneous","question":{"en":"Which ancient route did Sher Shah Suri reconstruct and extend under the name Sadak-e-Azam? [SSC CGL 12/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"शेरशाह सूरी ने \"सड़क-ए-आज़म\" नाम से किस प्राचीन मार्ग का पुनर्निर्माण व विस्तार किया? [SSC CGL 12/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"A Silk Road trading route","hi":"रेशम मार्ग का व्यापारिक मार्ग"},"2":{"en":"An ancient Mauryan route","hi":"एक प्राचीन मौर्यकालीन मार्ग"},"3":{"en":"A provincial Maratha highway","hi":"एक प्रांतीय मराठा राजमार्ग"},"4":{"en":"A Mughal military bypass","hi":"एक मुगल सैन्य बाईपास"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (2) – An ancient Mauryan route</b><br>Sher Shah Suri rebuilt and extended the ancient <b>Mauryan route</b> from the Kabul–Peshawar region through Punjab and Delhi to Bengal, naming it <b>Sadak-e-Azam</b> (the Great Road). It later came to be known as the <b>Grand Trunk Road</b>.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• The road ran from <b>Sonargaon in Bengal to Peshawar</b> (about 2,500 km) and had kos minars, sarais (rest houses) and trees along the way.<br>• Sher Shah built the <b>Purana Qila</b> at Delhi and the Rohtas Fort, and his revenue reforms introduced the <b>ryotwari-style patta and qabuliyat</b> system and the rupiya coin.<br>• The Grand Trunk Road was improved later by the British, and the <b>Sadak-e-Azam</b> remains one of Asia’s oldest and longest trade routes.<br>• Sher Shah ruled from <b>1540 to 1545</b> after defeating Humayun at Chausa and Kannauj, and was succeeded by Islam Shah Suri.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (2) – एक प्राचीन मौर्यकालीन मार्ग</b><br>शेरशाह सूरी ने काबुल–पेशावर क्षेत्र से पंजाब व दिल्ली होकर बंगाल तक जाने वाले प्राचीन <b>मौर्यकालीन मार्ग</b> का पुनर्निर्माण व विस्तार किया और उसे <b>सड़क-ए-आज़म</b> (महामार्ग) नाम दिया। बाद में यह <b>ग्रैंड ट्रंक रोड</b> के नाम से प्रसिद्ध हुआ।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• यह मार्ग <b>बंगाल के सोनारगाँव से पेशावर</b> तक (लगभग 2,500 किमी) था और इस पर कोस मीनार, सराय (विश्रामगृह) तथा पेड़ लगाए गए।<br>• शेरशाह ने दिल्ली में <b>पुराना किला</b> तथा रोहतासगढ़ का किला बनवाया; उसके राजस्व सुधारों में <b>पट्टा व कबूलियत</b> व्यवस्था तथा रुपये का सिक्का सम्मिलित था।<br>• ग्रैंड ट्रंक रोड को बाद में अंग्रेजों ने सुधारा तथा <b>सड़क-ए-आज़म</b> एशिया के प्राचीनतम व सबसे लंबे व्यापार मार्गों में से एक है।<br>• चौसा व कन्नौज में हुमायूँ को पराजित करने के बाद शेरशाह ने <b>1540 से 1545</b> तक शासन किया और उसके बाद इस्लाम शाह सूरी गद्दी पर बैठा।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":49,"local_id":"50049","quid":"Q1000071129","section":"GK","topic":"Modern History: Miscellaneous","question":{"en":"What was the main reason behind the rise of the poligars against the East India Company in South India? [SSC CGL 12/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"दक्षिण भारत में ईस्ट इंडिया कंपनी के विरुद्ध पोलिगारों के विद्रोह का मुख्य कारण क्या था? [SSC CGL 12/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"They objected to losing their hereditary revenue rights and were first angered over increased taxation.","hi":"उन्होंने अपने वंशानुगत राजस्व अधिकार खोने पर आपत्ति की और सर्वप्रथम बढ़े कराधान से क्रुद्ध हुए।"},"2":{"en":"They objected to losing their hereditary sovereign status and were first angered over taxation.","hi":"उन्होंने अपनी वंशानुगत संप्रभु स्थिति खोने पर आपत्ति की और सर्वप्रथम कराधान से क्रुद्ध हुए।"},"3":{"en":"They objected to losing their hereditary military privileges and were first angered over Company interference.","hi":"उन्होंने अपने वंशानुगत सैन्य विशेषाधिकार खोने पर आपत्ति की और सर्वप्रथम कंपनी के हस्तक्षेप से क्रुद्ध हुए।"},"4":{"en":"They objected to losing their hereditary local authority and were first angered over British administrative control.","hi":"उन्होंने अपनी वंशानुगत स्थानीय सत्ता खोने पर आपत्ति की और सर्वप्रथम ब्रिटिश प्रशासनिक नियंत्रण से क्रुद्ध हुए।"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (2) – They objected to losing their hereditary sovereign status and were first angered over taxation.</b><br>The <b>poligars</b> (palaiyakkarars) of the Tamil country were hereditary military chiefs holding tracts of land in return for service. The Company’s revenue settlements and its attempt to convert them into ordinary zamindars threatened their <b>hereditary sovereign status</b>, and increased taxation provoked the revolts of the late 18th and early 19th centuries.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• The <b>Poligar Revolt (1801–05)</b> was led by chiefs such as <b>Veerapandiya Kattabomman</b> of Panchalankurichi and the Marudhu brothers, and was suppressed by the British.<br>• The poligars had earlier fought in the <b>Polygar Wars</b> after the Company acquired the Carnatic and imposed the permanent revenue system.<br>• The <b>South Indian Rebellion (1800–01)</b> of Dheeran Chinnamalai and others had similar grievances of lost rights and heavy revenue demand.<br>• Other early uprisings against the Company include the <b>Sanyasi rebellion (1760s–1800)</b> in Bengal and the <b>Paika rebellion (1817)</b> in Odisha under Bakshi Jagabandhu.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (2) – उन्होंने अपनी वंशानुगत संप्रभु स्थिति खोने पर आपत्ति की और सर्वप्रथम कराधान से क्रुद्ध हुए।</b><br>तमिल क्षेत्र के <b>पोलिगार</b> (पलैयक्कारर) वंशानुगत सैन्य सरदार थे, जो सेवा के बदले भूमि रखते थे। कंपनी की राजस्व व्यवस्थाओं तथा उन्हें साधारण जमींदार बनाने के प्रयास से उनकी <b>वंशानुगत संप्रभु स्थिति</b> को खतरा उत्पन्न हुआ और बढ़े कराधान ने 18वीं सदी के अंत व 19वीं शताब्दी के आरंभ के विद्रोहों को जन्म दिया।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• <b>पोलिगार विद्रोह (1801–05)</b> का नेतृत्व पांचालनकुरिची के <b>वीरपांडिय कट्टबोम्मन</b> तथा मरुधु बंधुओं ने किया, जिसे अंग्रेजों ने दबा दिया।<br>• कंपनी द्वारा कर्नाटक पर अधिकार तथा स्थायी राजस्व व्यवस्था लागू करने के बाद पोलिगारों ने <b>पोलिगार युद्ध</b> लड़े।<br>• <b>दक्षिण भारतीय विद्रोह (1800–01)</b> में धीरन चिन्नामलै आदि की भी अधिकार-हानि व भारी राजस्व माँग जैसी शिकायतें थीं।<br>• कंपनी के विरुद्ध अन्य आरंभिक विद्रोहों में बंगाल का <b>संन्यासी विद्रोह (1760–1800)</b> तथा बख्शी जगबंधु के नेतृत्व में ओडिशा का <b>पाइका विद्रोह (1817)</b> सम्मिलित हैं।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":50,"local_id":"50050","quid":"Q1000071130","section":"GK","topic":"Biology: Plant and Animal Kingdom","question":{"en":"Two identical green plants are kept under different environmental conditions. Plant A is exposed to sunlight, whereas Plant B is kept in complete darkness for one week. Plant B becomes weak and pale. What is the main reason for this change? [SSC CGL 12/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"दो समान हरे पौधों को भिन्न पर्यावरणीय परिस्थितियों में रखा गया है। पौधा A सूर्य के प्रकाश के संपर्क में है, जबकि पौधा B को एक सप्ताह तक पूर्ण अंधकार में रखा गया है। पौधा B कमजोर व पीला पड़ जाता है। इस परिवर्तन का मुख्य कारण क्या है? [SSC CGL 12/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Absence of respiration","hi":"श्वसन का अभाव"},"2":{"en":"Excess production of oxygen","hi":"ऑक्सीजन का अत्यधिक उत्पादन"},"3":{"en":"Absence of photosynthesis","hi":"प्रकाश संश्लेषण का अभाव"},"4":{"en":"Excess production of chlorophyll","hi":"क्लोरोफिल का अत्यधिक उत्पादन"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (3) – Absence of photosynthesis</b><br>In complete darkness, Plant B cannot carry out <b>photosynthesis</b> because light is essential for the light reaction in the chloroplast. Without photosynthesis there is no new food or chlorophyll, so the plant becomes weak and pale — a condition called <b>etiolation</b>.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• Photosynthesis uses carbon dioxide, water and light in the presence of <b>chlorophyll</b> to produce glucose and oxygen: \\(6CO_2 + 6H_2O \\rightarrow C_6H_{12}O_6 + 6O_2\\).<br>• It occurs in the <b>chloroplast</b> — the light reaction in the grana and the Calvin cycle (dark reaction) in the stroma.<br>• Plants kept in darkness show <b>etiolation</b> — long, weak stems, small unopened leaves and loss of green colour.<br>• Respiration continues in both light and darkness, so it is not the cause of the pale colour; lack of chlorophyll and food is.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (3) – प्रकाश संश्लेषण का अभाव</b><br>पूर्ण अंधकार में पौधा B <b>प्रकाश संश्लेषण</b> नहीं कर सकता, क्योंकि हरितलवक की प्रकाश अभिक्रिया हेतु प्रकाश आवश्यक है। प्रकाश संश्लेषण के अभाव में नया भोजन व क्लोरोफिल नहीं बनता, अतः पौधा कमजोर व पीला पड़ जाता है — इस स्थिति को <b>एटियोलेशन (पीलापन)</b> कहते हैं।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• प्रकाश संश्लेषण में <b>क्लोरोफिल</b> की उपस्थिति में कार्बन डाइऑक्साइड, जल व प्रकाश से ग्लूकोज व ऑक्सीजन बनते हैं: \\(6CO_2 + 6H_2O \\rightarrow C_6H_{12}O_6 + 6O_2\\)।<br>• यह <b>हरितलवक</b> में होता है — प्रकाश अभिक्रिया ग्रेना में तथा कैल्विन चक्र (अप्रकाश अभिक्रिया) स्ट्रोमा में।<br>• अंधकार में रखे पौधों में <b>एटियोलेशन</b> दिखता है — लंबे कमजोर तने, छोटी बंद पत्तियाँ तथा हरा रंग समाप्त।<br>• श्वसन प्रकाश व अंधकार दोनों में चलता रहता है, अतः पीलापन उससे नहीं होता; इसका कारण क्लोरोफिल व भोजन की कमी है।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false}]},"MATH":{"seconds":900,"questions":[{"no":51,"local_id":"50051","quid":"Q1000071131","section":"MATH","topic":"Mensuration (3D)","question":{"en":"A solid metallic hemisphere of radius 6.3 cm is melted and recast into a right circular cylinder of radius 9 cm. What is the height of the cylinder? [SSC CGL 12/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"6.3 cm त्रिज्या वाले धातु के एक ठोस अर्धगोले को पिघलाकर 9 cm त्रिज्या वाले एक लंब वृत्तीय बेलन में ढाला जाता है। बेलन की ऊँचाई क्या है? [SSC CGL 12/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"1.058 cm"},"2":{"en":"2.058 cm"},"3":{"en":"2.58 cm"},"4":{"en":"3.058 cm"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<svg width=\"135\" height=\"105\" viewBox=\"0 0 135 105\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" font-size=\"12\"><path d=\"M15 40a50 50 0 0 0 100 0\"/><ellipse cx=\"65\" cy=\"40\" rx=\"50\" ry=\"12\"/><path stroke-dasharray=\"4 3\" d=\"M65 40H115\"/><g fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\"><text x=\"90\" y=\"56\" text-anchor=\"middle\">6.3</text></g></svg>&nbsp; <svg width=\"170\" height=\"140\" viewBox=\"0 0 170 140\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" font-size=\"12\"><ellipse cx=\"70\" cy=\"22\" rx=\"50\" ry=\"12\"/><path d=\"M20 22V112M120 22V112M20 112a50 12 0 0 0 100 0\"/><path stroke-dasharray=\"4 3\" d=\"M20 112a50 12 0 0 1 100 0M70 22H120M70 22V112\"/><g fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\"><text x=\"84\" y=\"31\">9</text><text x=\"126\" y=\"72\">h</text></g></svg><br>Volume of hemisphere = Volume of cylinder<br>\\(\\frac{2}{3}\\pi (6.3)^3 = \\pi (9)^2 h\\)<br>\\(h = \\frac{2 \\times 250.047}{3 \\times 81} = \\frac{166.698}{81}\\)<br>\\(h = \\boxed{2.058}\\) cm<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): 2.058 cm.</b>","hi":"<svg width=\"135\" height=\"105\" viewBox=\"0 0 135 105\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" font-size=\"12\"><path d=\"M15 40a50 50 0 0 0 100 0\"/><ellipse cx=\"65\" cy=\"40\" rx=\"50\" ry=\"12\"/><path stroke-dasharray=\"4 3\" d=\"M65 40H115\"/><g fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\"><text x=\"90\" y=\"56\" text-anchor=\"middle\">6.3</text></g></svg>&nbsp; <svg width=\"170\" height=\"140\" viewBox=\"0 0 170 140\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" font-size=\"12\"><ellipse cx=\"70\" cy=\"22\" rx=\"50\" ry=\"12\"/><path d=\"M20 22V112M120 22V112M20 112a50 12 0 0 0 100 0\"/><path stroke-dasharray=\"4 3\" d=\"M20 112a50 12 0 0 1 100 0M70 22H120M70 22V112\"/><g fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\"><text x=\"84\" y=\"31\">9</text><text x=\"126\" y=\"72\">h</text></g></svg><br>अर्धगोले का आयतन = बेलन का आयतन<br>\\(\\frac{2}{3}\\pi (6.3)^3 = \\pi (9)^2 h\\)<br>\\(h = \\frac{2 \\times 250.047}{3 \\times 81} = \\frac{166.698}{81}\\)<br>\\(h = \\boxed{2.058}\\) cm<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): 2.058 cm है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":52,"local_id":"50052","quid":"Q1000071132","section":"MATH","topic":"Geometry","question":{"en":"A triangle has side lengths of 7 cm, 24 cm, and 25 cm. Determine the circumradius of the triangle. [SSC CGL 12/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"एक त्रिभुज की भुजाओं की लंबाई 7 cm, 24 cm और 25 cm है। त्रिभुज की परित्रिज्या ज्ञात कीजिए। [SSC CGL 12/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"12.5 cm"},"2":{"en":"13.5 cm"},"3":{"en":"14 cm"},"4":{"en":"16 cm"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<svg width=\"212\" height=\"212\" viewBox=\"0 0 212 212\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" font-size=\"12\"><path d=\"M39 63L26 106L186 106ZM37 70L43 72L45 65\"/><circle cx=\"106\" cy=\"106\" r=\"80\"/><circle cx=\"106\" cy=\"106\" r=\"2\" fill=\"#000\"/><g fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3\" paint-order=\"stroke\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" text-anchor=\"middle\"><text x=\"36\" y=\"60\">A</text><text x=\"16\" y=\"110\">B</text><text x=\"196\" y=\"110\">C</text><text x=\"106\" y=\"122\">O</text><text x=\"20\" y=\"85\">7</text><text x=\"116\" y=\"75\">24</text><text x=\"148\" y=\"122\" font-size=\"11\">25</text></g></svg><br>\\(7^2 + 24^2 = 49 + 576 = 625 = 25^2\\) → right-angled triangle (∠A = 90°)<br>Circumradius of a right triangle = \\(\\frac{\\text{Hypotenuse}}{2}\\)<br>\\(R = \\frac{25}{2} = \\boxed{12.5}\\) cm<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): 12.5 cm.</b>","hi":"<svg width=\"212\" height=\"212\" viewBox=\"0 0 212 212\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" font-size=\"12\"><path d=\"M39 63L26 106L186 106ZM37 70L43 72L45 65\"/><circle cx=\"106\" cy=\"106\" r=\"80\"/><circle cx=\"106\" cy=\"106\" r=\"2\" fill=\"#000\"/><g fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3\" paint-order=\"stroke\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" text-anchor=\"middle\"><text x=\"36\" y=\"60\">A</text><text x=\"16\" y=\"110\">B</text><text x=\"196\" y=\"110\">C</text><text x=\"106\" y=\"122\">O</text><text x=\"20\" y=\"85\">7</text><text x=\"116\" y=\"75\">24</text><text x=\"148\" y=\"122\" font-size=\"11\">25</text></g></svg><br>\\(7^2 + 24^2 = 49 + 576 = 625 = 25^2\\) → समकोण त्रिभुज (∠A = 90°)<br>समकोण त्रिभुज की परित्रिज्या = \\(\\frac{\\text{Hypotenuse}}{2}\\)<br>\\(R = \\frac{25}{2} = \\boxed{12.5}\\) cm<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (1): 12.5 cm है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":53,"local_id":"50053","quid":"Q1000071133","section":"MATH","topic":"Geometry","question":{"en":"In a regular polygon, each interior angle exceeds its corresponding exterior angle by 132°. Find the number of sides of the polygon. [SSC CGL 12/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"एक सम बहुभुज में, प्रत्येक आंतरिक कोण अपने संगत बाह्य कोण से 132° अधिक है। बहुभुज की भुजाओं की संख्या ज्ञात कीजिए। [SSC CGL 12/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"17"},"2":{"en":"18"},"3":{"en":"15"},"4":{"en":"16"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"Interior + Exterior = 180°, Interior − Exterior = 132°<br>Exterior = \\(\\frac{180^\\circ - 132^\\circ}{2} = 24^\\circ\\)<br>Number of sides = \\(\\frac{360^\\circ}{24^\\circ} = \\boxed{15}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): 15.</b>","hi":"आंतरिक + बाह्य = 180°, आंतरिक − बाह्य = 132°<br>बाह्य कोण = \\(\\frac{180^\\circ - 132^\\circ}{2} = 24^\\circ\\)<br>भुजाओं की संख्या = \\(\\frac{360^\\circ}{24^\\circ} = \\boxed{15}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (3): 15 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":54,"local_id":"50054","quid":"Q1000071134","section":"MATH","topic":"Elementary Statistics","question":{"en":"Examine the frequency polygon on math Exam Scores (out of 100), Groups: Batch A vs. Batch B and answer the following question.<br>Which batch has a higher average (approximate) score, assuming midpoints represent class scores?<br><img src=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-12-OCT-2026-SHIFT-3/q54.jpg\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\"> [SSC CGL 12/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"गणित परीक्षा अंकों (100 में से) पर आधारित आवृत्ति बहुभुज, समूह: बैच A बनाम बैच B, का अध्ययन कीजिए और निम्नलिखित प्रश्न का उत्तर दीजिए।<br>यह मानते हुए कि मध्य-बिंदु वर्ग के अंकों को दर्शाते हैं, किस बैच का औसत (लगभग) अंक अधिक है?<br><img src=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-12-OCT-2026-SHIFT-3/q54.jpg\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\"> [SSC CGL 12/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Batch A","hi":"बैच A"},"2":{"en":"Batch B","hi":"बैच B"},"3":{"en":"Both have equal average","hi":"दोनों का औसत बराबर है"},"4":{"en":"Cannot be determined","hi":"निर्धारित नहीं किया जा सकता"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<table style=\"border-collapse:collapse\"><tr><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">Mid-point</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">10</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">30</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">50</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">70</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">90</td></tr><tr><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">Batch A</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">5</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">12</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">25</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">18</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">10</td></tr><tr><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">Batch B</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">10</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">18</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">22</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">15</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">5</td></tr></table>Both batches have total frequency 70.<br>A: \\(\\frac{50 + 360 + 1250 + 1260 + 900}{70} = \\frac{3820}{70} \\approx 54.6\\)<br>B: \\(\\frac{100 + 540 + 1100 + 1050 + 450}{70} = \\frac{3240}{70} \\approx 46.3\\)<br>Higher average: \\(\\boxed{\\text{Batch A}}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): Batch A.</b>","hi":"<table style=\"border-collapse:collapse\"><tr><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">मध्य-बिंदु</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">10</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">30</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">50</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">70</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">90</td></tr><tr><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">बैच A</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">5</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">12</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">25</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">18</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">10</td></tr><tr><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">बैच B</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">10</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">18</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">22</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">15</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">5</td></tr></table>दोनों बैचों की कुल आवृत्ति 70 है।<br>A: \\(\\frac{50 + 360 + 1250 + 1260 + 900}{70} = \\frac{3820}{70} \\approx 54.6\\)<br>B: \\(\\frac{100 + 540 + 1100 + 1050 + 450}{70} = \\frac{3240}{70} \\approx 46.3\\)<br>अधिक औसत: \\(\\boxed{\\text{Batch A}}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (1): बैच A है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":true,"images":{"question":["https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-12-OCT-2026-SHIFT-3/q54.jpg"]}},{"no":55,"local_id":"50055","quid":"Q1000071135","section":"MATH","topic":"Trigonometry","question":{"en":"If tanθ = 3/4, find the value of (1 + sinθ)(1 − sinθ). [SSC CGL 12/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"यदि tanθ = 3/4 है, तो (1 + sinθ)(1 − sinθ) का मान ज्ञात कीजिए। [SSC CGL 12/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"7/25"},"2":{"en":"9/25"},"3":{"en":"16/25"},"4":{"en":"1"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"\\(\\tan\\theta = \\frac{3}{4}\\) → P = 3, B = 4, H = 5 → \\(\\cos\\theta = \\frac{4}{5}\\)<br>\\((1 + \\sin\\theta)(1 - \\sin\\theta) = 1 - \\sin^2\\theta = \\cos^2\\theta\\)<br>\\(= \\left(\\frac{4}{5}\\right)^2 = \\boxed{\\frac{16}{25}}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): 16/25.</b>","hi":"\\(\\tan\\theta = \\frac{3}{4}\\) → लंब = 3, आधार = 4, कर्ण = 5 → \\(\\cos\\theta = \\frac{4}{5}\\)<br>\\((1 + \\sin\\theta)(1 - \\sin\\theta) = 1 - \\sin^2\\theta = \\cos^2\\theta\\)<br>\\(= \\left(\\frac{4}{5}\\right)^2 = \\boxed{\\frac{16}{25}}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (3): 16/25 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":56,"local_id":"50056","quid":"Q1000071136","section":"MATH","topic":"Data Interpretation (DI)","question":{"en":"Using the provided bar graph, which shows the quantity of fruit sold in kilograms, answer the following questions.<br>If the fruits are ranked based on descending order of quantity sold, what is the ratio of the combined sales of the top two fruits to the bottom two?<br><img src=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-12-OCT-2026-SHIFT-3/q56.jpg\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\"> [SSC CGL 12/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"दिए गए दंड आलेख, जो किलोग्राम में बेचे गए फलों की मात्रा दर्शाता है, का उपयोग करके निम्नलिखित प्रश्नों के उत्तर दीजिए।<br>यदि फलों को बेची गई मात्रा के अवरोही क्रम में रखा जाए, तो शीर्ष दो फलों की संयुक्त बिक्री और निचले दो फलों की संयुक्त बिक्री का अनुपात क्या है?<br><img src=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-12-OCT-2026-SHIFT-3/q56.jpg\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\"> [SSC CGL 12/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"9:5"},"2":{"en":"11:5"},"3":{"en":"7:3"},"4":{"en":"5:2"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"From the graph: Bananas 150, Apples 120, Mangoes 100, Oranges 90, Grapes 60 (kg)<br>Top two = 150 + 120 = 270; Bottom two = 90 + 60 = 150<br>Ratio = 270 : 150 = \\(\\boxed{9 : 5}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): 9:5.</b>","hi":"आलेख से: केले 150, सेब 120, आम 100, संतरे 90, अंगूर 60 (kg)<br>शीर्ष दो = 150 + 120 = 270; निचले दो = 90 + 60 = 150<br>अनुपात = 270 : 150 = \\(\\boxed{9 : 5}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (1): 9:5 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":true,"images":{"question":["https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-12-OCT-2026-SHIFT-3/q56.jpg"]}},{"no":57,"local_id":"50057","quid":"Q1000071137","section":"MATH","topic":"Data Interpretation (DI)","question":{"en":"Examine the bar graph below to, answer the following question.<br>What is the average female literacy rate across the five listed states?<br><img src=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-12-OCT-2026-SHIFT-3/q57.jpg\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\"> [SSC CGL 12/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"नीचे दिए गए दंड आलेख का अध्ययन करके निम्नलिखित प्रश्न का उत्तर दीजिए।<br>सूचीबद्ध पाँच राज्यों में औसत महिला साक्षरता दर क्या है?<br><img src=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-12-OCT-2026-SHIFT-3/q57.jpg\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\"> [SSC CGL 12/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"76.2%"},"2":{"en":"75.8%"},"3":{"en":"77.4%"},"4":{"en":"78.0%"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"Female literacy from the graph: Kerala 96, Rajasthan 60, Bihar 55, Tamil Nadu 88, Gujarat 82<br>Sum = 381<br>Average = \\(\\frac{381}{5} = \\boxed{76.2\\%}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): 76.2%.</b>","hi":"आलेख से महिला साक्षरता: केरल 96, राजस्थान 60, बिहार 55, तमिलनाडु 88, गुजरात 82<br>योग = 381<br>औसत = \\(\\frac{381}{5} = \\boxed{76.2\\%}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (1): 76.2% है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":true,"images":{"question":["https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-12-OCT-2026-SHIFT-3/q57.jpg"]}},{"no":58,"local_id":"50058","quid":"Q1000071138","section":"MATH","topic":"Data Interpretation (DI)","question":{"en":"Carefully study the pie chart showing the distribution of favorite colors. Then answer the following questions.<br>Assume the total number of respondents shown in the chart is <b>1,000</b>. If <b>10%</b> of people who preferred <b>Red</b> switch to <b>Yellow</b>, and <b>20%</b> of people who preferred <b>Other</b> switch to <b>Blue</b>, what will be the new percentage of people who prefer <b>Blue</b>?<br><img src=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-12-OCT-2026-SHIFT-3/q58.jpg\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\"> [SSC CGL 12/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"पसंदीदा रंगों के वितरण को दर्शाने वाले पाई चार्ट का ध्यानपूर्वक अध्ययन कीजिए। फिर निम्नलिखित प्रश्नों के उत्तर दीजिए।<br>मान लीजिए चार्ट में दर्शाए गए उत्तरदाताओं की कुल संख्या <b>1,000</b> है। यदि <b>लाल</b> पसंद करने वाले <b>10%</b> लोग <b>पीला</b> पसंद करने लगें, और <b>अन्य</b> पसंद करने वाले <b>20%</b> लोग <b>नीला</b> पसंद करने लगें, तो <b>नीला</b> पसंद करने वाले लोगों का नया प्रतिशत क्या होगा?<br><img src=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-12-OCT-2026-SHIFT-3/q58.jpg\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\"> [SSC CGL 12/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"32%"},"2":{"en":"34%"},"3":{"en":"36%"},"4":{"en":"38%"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"From the chart: Blue 30%, Other 10% of 1000<br>Blue = 300, Other = 100<br>20% of Other move to Blue = 20 → Blue = 320 (Red → Yellow does not affect Blue)<br>New Blue % = \\(\\frac{320}{1000} \\times 100 = \\boxed{32\\%}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): 32%.</b>","hi":"चार्ट से: नीला 30%, अन्य 10% (1000 में से)<br>नीला = 300, अन्य = 100<br>अन्य के 20% नीला में = 20 → नीला = 320 (लाल → पीला से नीला पर प्रभाव नहीं)<br>नीला का नया % = \\(\\frac{320}{1000} \\times 100 = \\boxed{32\\%}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (1): 32% है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":true,"images":{"question":["https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-12-OCT-2026-SHIFT-3/q58.jpg"]}},{"no":59,"local_id":"50059","quid":"Q1000071139","section":"MATH","topic":"Simplification and Approximation","question":{"en":"<b>Evaluate:</b> \\(\\frac{(0.125 - 0.027)}{0.25 + 0.15 + 0.09}\\). [SSC CGL 12/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"<b>मान ज्ञात कीजिए:</b> \\(\\frac{(0.125 - 0.027)}{0.25 + 0.15 + 0.09}\\)। [SSC CGL 12/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"0.4"},"2":{"en":"0.2"},"3":{"en":"0.6"},"4":{"en":"0.8"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"Let a = 0.5, b = 0.3 → \\(a^3 = 0.125,\\ b^3 = 0.027,\\ a^2 = 0.25,\\ ab = 0.15,\\ b^2 = 0.09\\)<br>\\(\\frac{a^3 - b^3}{a^2 + ab + b^2} = a - b\\)<br>\\(= 0.5 - 0.3 = \\boxed{0.2}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): 0.2.</b>","hi":"माना a = 0.5, b = 0.3 → \\(a^3 = 0.125,\\ b^3 = 0.027,\\ a^2 = 0.25,\\ ab = 0.15,\\ b^2 = 0.09\\)<br>\\(\\frac{a^3 - b^3}{a^2 + ab + b^2} = a - b\\)<br>\\(= 0.5 - 0.3 = \\boxed{0.2}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): 0.2 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":60,"local_id":"50060","quid":"Q1000071140","section":"MATH","topic":"Simplification and Approximation","question":{"en":"Find the value of \\(\\frac{(0.013)^3 - (0.011)^3}{(0.013)^2 + 0.000143 + (0.011)^2}\\). [SSC CGL 12/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"\\(\\frac{(0.013)^3 - (0.011)^3}{(0.013)^2 + 0.000143 + (0.011)^2}\\) का मान ज्ञात कीजिए। [SSC CGL 12/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"0.004"},"2":{"en":"0.002"},"3":{"en":"0.006"},"4":{"en":"0.008"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"a = 0.013, b = 0.011 → ab = 0.000143<br>\\(\\frac{a^3 - b^3}{a^2 + ab + b^2} = a - b\\)<br>\\(= 0.013 - 0.011 = \\boxed{0.002}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): 0.002.</b>","hi":"a = 0.013, b = 0.011 → ab = 0.000143<br>\\(\\frac{a^3 - b^3}{a^2 + ab + b^2} = a - b\\)<br>\\(= 0.013 - 0.011 = \\boxed{0.002}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): 0.002 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":61,"local_id":"50061","quid":"Q1000071141","section":"MATH","topic":"Algebra","question":{"en":"If \\(2x = 0.5y\\), then find \\(\\frac{y^2 - x^2}{y^2 + 2xy + x^2}\\). [SSC CGL 12/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"यदि \\(2x = 0.5y\\) है, तो \\(\\frac{y^2 - x^2}{y^2 + 2xy + x^2}\\) ज्ञात कीजिए। [SSC CGL 12/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"\\(\\frac{2}{5}\\)"},"2":{"en":"\\(\\frac{4}{5}\\)"},"3":{"en":"\\(\\frac{3}{5}\\)"},"4":{"en":"\\(\\frac{7}{5}\\)"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"\\(2x = 0.5y \\Rightarrow y = 4x\\)<br>\\(\\frac{y^2 - x^2}{(y + x)^2} = \\frac{y - x}{y + x} = \\frac{4x - x}{4x + x}\\)<br>\\(= \\boxed{\\frac{3}{5}}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): \\(\\frac{3}{5}\\).</b>","hi":"\\(2x = 0.5y \\Rightarrow y = 4x\\)<br>\\(\\frac{y^2 - x^2}{(y + x)^2} = \\frac{y - x}{y + x} = \\frac{4x - x}{4x + x}\\)<br>\\(= \\boxed{\\frac{3}{5}}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (3): \\(\\frac{3}{5}\\) है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":62,"local_id":"50062","quid":"Q1000071142","section":"MATH","topic":"Number System","question":{"en":"Find the value of (x + y) if 5x2y1 is divisible by 3 and x and y are the same digit. [SSC CGL 12/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"यदि 5x2y1, 3 से विभाज्य है और x तथा y एक ही अंक हैं, तो (x + y) का मान ज्ञात कीजिए। [SSC CGL 12/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"4"},"2":{"en":"8"},"3":{"en":"36"},"4":{"en":"34"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"Sum of digits = 5 + x + 2 + x + 1 = 8 + 2x must be divisible by 3<br>x = 2 → 12 ✔ (x = 5 → 18, x = 8 → 24 also work, giving 10 and 16, not in options)<br>x + y = 2 + 2 = \\(\\boxed{4}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): 4.</b>","hi":"अंकों का योग = 5 + x + 2 + x + 1 = 8 + 2x, 3 से विभाज्य होना चाहिए<br>x = 2 → 12 ✔ (x = 5 → 18, x = 8 → 24 भी संभव, जिनसे 10 और 16 मिलते हैं, जो विकल्पों में नहीं हैं)<br>x + y = 2 + 2 = \\(\\boxed{4}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (1): 4 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":63,"local_id":"50063","quid":"Q1000071143","section":"MATH","topic":"Geometry","question":{"en":"In ΔWTQ, ∠W = 50°, ∠T = 70°, and the bisectors of ∠T and ∠Q meet at R. Find ∠TRQ. [SSC CGL 12/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"ΔWTQ में, ∠W = 50°, ∠T = 70° है, और ∠T तथा ∠Q के समद्विभाजक R पर मिलते हैं। ∠TRQ ज्ञात कीजिए। [SSC CGL 12/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"143°"},"2":{"en":"125°"},"3":{"en":"105°"},"4":{"en":"115°"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"<svg width=\"177\" height=\"174\" viewBox=\"0 0 177 174\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" font-size=\"12\"><path d=\"M72 20L25 150H147Z\"/><path d=\"M25 150L80 111L147 150\"/><g fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\"><text x=\"72\" y=\"14\" text-anchor=\"middle\">W</text><text x=\"13\" y=\"154\">T</text><text x=\"151\" y=\"154\">Q</text><text x=\"75\" y=\"50\" text-anchor=\"middle\">50°</text><text x=\"46\" y=\"138\" text-anchor=\"middle\">70°</text><text x=\"126\" y=\"140\" text-anchor=\"middle\">60°</text><text x=\"80\" y=\"105\" text-anchor=\"middle\">R</text></g></svg><br>R is the point where internal bisectors of ∠T and ∠Q meet<br>\\(\\angle TRQ = 90^\\circ + \\frac{\\angle W}{2}\\)<br>\\(= 90^\\circ + 25^\\circ = \\boxed{115^\\circ}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): 115°.</b>","hi":"<svg width=\"177\" height=\"174\" viewBox=\"0 0 177 174\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" font-size=\"12\"><path d=\"M72 20L25 150H147Z\"/><path d=\"M25 150L80 111L147 150\"/><g fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\"><text x=\"72\" y=\"14\" text-anchor=\"middle\">W</text><text x=\"13\" y=\"154\">T</text><text x=\"151\" y=\"154\">Q</text><text x=\"75\" y=\"50\" text-anchor=\"middle\">50°</text><text x=\"46\" y=\"138\" text-anchor=\"middle\">70°</text><text x=\"126\" y=\"140\" text-anchor=\"middle\">60°</text><text x=\"80\" y=\"105\" text-anchor=\"middle\">R</text></g></svg><br>R वह बिंदु है जहाँ ∠T और ∠Q के आंतरिक समद्विभाजक मिलते हैं<br>\\(\\angle TRQ = 90^\\circ + \\frac{\\angle W}{2}\\)<br>\\(= 90^\\circ + 25^\\circ = \\boxed{115^\\circ}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (4): 115° है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":64,"local_id":"50064","quid":"Q1000071144","section":"MATH","topic":"Profit and Loss","question":{"en":"A man sells two articles for &#36;5000 each, making no overall profit or loss. If one article is sold at a 25% profit, what is the approximate percentage loss on the other article? [SSC CGL 12/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"एक व्यक्ति दो वस्तुएँ &#36;5000 प्रत्येक में बेचता है, और कुल मिलाकर न लाभ होता है न हानि। यदि एक वस्तु 25% लाभ पर बेची जाती है, तो दूसरी वस्तु पर लगभग कितने प्रतिशत हानि हुई? [SSC CGL 12/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"14.56%"},"2":{"en":"16.67%"},"3":{"en":"12.28%"},"4":{"en":"11.42%"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"CP of first = \\(\\frac{5000}{125} \\times 100 = 4000\\)<br>No profit no loss → total CP = total SP = 10000 → CP of second = 6000<br>Loss = 1000 → Loss % = \\(\\frac{1000}{6000} \\times 100 = \\boxed{16.67\\%}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): 16.67%.</b>","hi":"पहली वस्तु का क्रय मूल्य = \\(\\frac{5000}{125} \\times 100 = 4000\\)<br>न लाभ न हानि → कुल क्रय मूल्य = कुल विक्रय मूल्य = 10000 → दूसरी का क्रय मूल्य = 6000<br>हानि = 1000 → हानि % = \\(\\frac{1000}{6000} \\times 100 = \\boxed{16.67\\%}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): 16.67% है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":65,"local_id":"50065","quid":"Q1000071145","section":"MATH","topic":"Geometry","question":{"en":"A chord AB of a circle subtends an angle of 55° at a point on the major arc. What is the angle subtended by the same chord at the centre of the circle? [SSC CGL 12/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"एक वृत्त की जीवा AB दीर्घ चाप पर स्थित एक बिंदु पर 55° का कोण बनाती है। वही जीवा वृत्त के केंद्र पर कितना कोण बनाती है? [SSC CGL 12/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"55°"},"2":{"en":"117.5°"},"3":{"en":"110°"},"4":{"en":"125°"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<svg width=\"165\" height=\"150\" viewBox=\"0 0 165 150\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" font-size=\"12\"><circle cx=\"80\" cy=\"75\" r=\"55\"/><path d=\"M35 107L80 20L125 107ZM35 107L80 75L125 107\"/><circle cx=\"80\" cy=\"75\" r=\"1.5\" fill=\"#000\"/><g fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\"><text x=\"74\" y=\"73\" text-anchor=\"end\">O</text><text x=\"31\" y=\"119\" text-anchor=\"end\">A</text><text x=\"129\" y=\"119\">B</text><text x=\"80\" y=\"15\" text-anchor=\"middle\">P</text><text x=\"80\" y=\"46\" text-anchor=\"middle\">55°</text><text x=\"80\" y=\"97\" text-anchor=\"middle\">?</text></g></svg><br>Angle at the centre = 2 × angle on the major arc<br>\\(\\angle AOB = 2 \\times 55^\\circ = \\boxed{110^\\circ}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): 110°.</b>","hi":"<svg width=\"165\" height=\"150\" viewBox=\"0 0 165 150\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" font-size=\"12\"><circle cx=\"80\" cy=\"75\" r=\"55\"/><path d=\"M35 107L80 20L125 107ZM35 107L80 75L125 107\"/><circle cx=\"80\" cy=\"75\" r=\"1.5\" fill=\"#000\"/><g fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\"><text x=\"74\" y=\"73\" text-anchor=\"end\">O</text><text x=\"31\" y=\"119\" text-anchor=\"end\">A</text><text x=\"129\" y=\"119\">B</text><text x=\"80\" y=\"15\" text-anchor=\"middle\">P</text><text x=\"80\" y=\"46\" text-anchor=\"middle\">55°</text><text x=\"80\" y=\"97\" text-anchor=\"middle\">?</text></g></svg><br>केंद्र पर कोण = 2 × दीर्घ चाप पर कोण<br>\\(\\angle AOB = 2 \\times 55^\\circ = \\boxed{110^\\circ}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (3): 110° है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":66,"local_id":"50066","quid":"Q1000071146","section":"MATH","topic":"Height and Distance","question":{"en":"Two ships on the same side of a lighthouse observe angles 30° and 45°. The lighthouse height is 80 m. Find the approximate distance between ships. Take \\((\\sqrt{3} = 1.732)\\) [SSC CGL 12/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"एक प्रकाशस्तंभ के एक ही ओर स्थित दो जहाज़ 30° और 45° के कोण देखते हैं। प्रकाशस्तंभ की ऊँचाई 80 m है। जहाज़ों के बीच की लगभग दूरी ज्ञात कीजिए। \\((\\sqrt{3} = 1.732)\\) लीजिए। [SSC CGL 12/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"59 m"},"2":{"en":"49 m"},"3":{"en":"50 m"},"4":{"en":"63 m"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<svg width=\"262\" height=\"159\" viewBox=\"0 0 262 159\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" font-size=\"12\"><path d=\"M50 20V124H230ZM50 20L154 124\"/><path d=\"M50 116h8v8\"/><path d=\"M138 124A16 16 0 0 1 143 113\"/><path d=\"M214 124A16 16 0 0 1 216 116\"/><path d=\"M154 143H230\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><g fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\"><text x=\"45\" y=\"24\" text-anchor=\"end\">A</text><text x=\"45\" y=\"128\" text-anchor=\"end\">B</text><text x=\"154\" y=\"138\" text-anchor=\"middle\">D</text><text x=\"230\" y=\"138\" text-anchor=\"middle\">C</text><text x=\"45\" y=\"76\" text-anchor=\"end\">80 m</text><text x=\"157\" y=\"118\">45°</text><text x=\"233\" y=\"118\">30°</text><text x=\"192\" y=\"153\" text-anchor=\"middle\">x</text></g></svg><br>BD = \\(\\frac{80}{\\tan 45^\\circ} = 80\\) m<br>BC = \\(\\frac{80}{\\tan 30^\\circ} = 80\\sqrt{3} = 138.56\\) m<br>x = CD = \\(138.56 - 80 = 58.56 \\approx \\boxed{59}\\) m<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): 59 m.</b>","hi":"<svg width=\"262\" height=\"159\" viewBox=\"0 0 262 159\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" font-size=\"12\"><path d=\"M50 20V124H230ZM50 20L154 124\"/><path d=\"M50 116h8v8\"/><path d=\"M138 124A16 16 0 0 1 143 113\"/><path d=\"M214 124A16 16 0 0 1 216 116\"/><path d=\"M154 143H230\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><g fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\"><text x=\"45\" y=\"24\" text-anchor=\"end\">A</text><text x=\"45\" y=\"128\" text-anchor=\"end\">B</text><text x=\"154\" y=\"138\" text-anchor=\"middle\">D</text><text x=\"230\" y=\"138\" text-anchor=\"middle\">C</text><text x=\"45\" y=\"76\" text-anchor=\"end\">80 m</text><text x=\"157\" y=\"118\">45°</text><text x=\"233\" y=\"118\">30°</text><text x=\"192\" y=\"153\" text-anchor=\"middle\">x</text></g></svg><br>BD = \\(\\frac{80}{\\tan 45^\\circ} = 80\\) m<br>BC = \\(\\frac{80}{\\tan 30^\\circ} = 80\\sqrt{3} = 138.56\\) m<br>x = CD = \\(138.56 - 80 = 58.56 \\approx \\boxed{59}\\) m<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (1): 59 m है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":67,"local_id":"50067","quid":"Q1000071147","section":"MATH","topic":"Mensuration (2D)","question":{"en":"When the diagonal of a square is increased by 20%, what is the percentage increase in the area of the square? [SSC CGL 12/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"जब एक वर्ग के विकर्ण में 20% की वृद्धि की जाती है, तो वर्ग के क्षेत्रफल में कितने प्रतिशत की वृद्धि होती है? [SSC CGL 12/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"20%"},"2":{"en":"40%"},"3":{"en":"44%"},"4":{"en":"50%"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<svg width=\"150\" height=\"140\" viewBox=\"0 0 150 140\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" font-size=\"12\"><path d=\"M20 20H120V120H20Z\"/><path stroke-dasharray=\"4 3\" d=\"M20 120L120 20\"/><g fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\"><text x=\"74\" y=\"64\">d</text><text x=\"70\" y=\"135\" text-anchor=\"middle\">a</text></g></svg><br>Area = \\(\\frac{d^2}{2}\\) → Area ∝ d²<br>New area = \\((1.2)^2 = 1.44\\) times<br>Increase = \\(\\boxed{44\\%}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): 44%.</b>","hi":"<svg width=\"150\" height=\"140\" viewBox=\"0 0 150 140\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" font-size=\"12\"><path d=\"M20 20H120V120H20Z\"/><path stroke-dasharray=\"4 3\" d=\"M20 120L120 20\"/><g fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\"><text x=\"74\" y=\"64\">d</text><text x=\"70\" y=\"135\" text-anchor=\"middle\">a</text></g></svg><br>क्षेत्रफल = \\(\\frac{d^2}{2}\\) → क्षेत्रफल ∝ d²<br>नया क्षेत्रफल = \\((1.2)^2 = 1.44\\) गुना<br>वृद्धि = \\(\\boxed{44\\%}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (3): 44% है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":68,"local_id":"50068","quid":"Q1000071148","section":"MATH","topic":"Geometry","question":{"en":"A chord of a circle subtends 45° at the circumference. If the chord length is 8 cm, find the distance from the centre to the chord. [SSC CGL 12/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"एक वृत्त की जीवा परिधि पर 45° का कोण बनाती है। यदि जीवा की लंबाई 8 cm है, तो केंद्र से जीवा की दूरी ज्ञात कीजिए। [SSC CGL 12/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"2 cm"},"2":{"en":"\\(2\\sqrt{2}\\) cm"},"3":{"en":"4 cm"},"4":{"en":"\\(4\\sqrt{2}\\) cm"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<svg width=\"232\" height=\"232\" viewBox=\"0 0 232 232\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" font-size=\"12\"><path d=\"M52 180L180 180M116 116L116 180M123 180L123 173L116 173M52 180L100 27L180 180M96 43A16 16 0 0 0 108 42\"/><path stroke-dasharray=\"4 3\" d=\"M116 116L180 180\"/><circle cx=\"116\" cy=\"116\" r=\"90\"/><circle cx=\"116\" cy=\"116\" r=\"2\" fill=\"#000\"/><g fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3\" paint-order=\"stroke\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" text-anchor=\"middle\"><text x=\"108\" y=\"110\">O</text><text x=\"42\" y=\"194\">A</text><text x=\"190\" y=\"194\">B</text><text x=\"116\" y=\"196\">M</text><text x=\"111\" y=\"152\" text-anchor=\"end\" font-size=\"11\">d</text><text x=\"148\" y=\"176\" font-size=\"11\">4</text><text x=\"142\" y=\"158\">r</text><text x=\"100\" y=\"24\">P</text><text x=\"103\" y=\"59\" font-size=\"11\">45°</text></g></svg><br>Angle at centre = 2 × 45° = 90° → ΔOAB is right-angled isosceles<br>OM bisects the chord and \\(\\angle BOM = 45^\\circ\\), so OM = MB<br>d = OM = \\(\\frac{8}{2} = \\boxed{4}\\) cm<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): 4 cm.</b>","hi":"<svg width=\"232\" height=\"232\" viewBox=\"0 0 232 232\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" font-size=\"12\"><path d=\"M52 180L180 180M116 116L116 180M123 180L123 173L116 173M52 180L100 27L180 180M96 43A16 16 0 0 0 108 42\"/><path stroke-dasharray=\"4 3\" d=\"M116 116L180 180\"/><circle cx=\"116\" cy=\"116\" r=\"90\"/><circle cx=\"116\" cy=\"116\" r=\"2\" fill=\"#000\"/><g fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3\" paint-order=\"stroke\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" text-anchor=\"middle\"><text x=\"108\" y=\"110\">O</text><text x=\"42\" y=\"194\">A</text><text x=\"190\" y=\"194\">B</text><text x=\"116\" y=\"196\">M</text><text x=\"111\" y=\"152\" text-anchor=\"end\" font-size=\"11\">d</text><text x=\"148\" y=\"176\" font-size=\"11\">4</text><text x=\"142\" y=\"158\">r</text><text x=\"100\" y=\"24\">P</text><text x=\"103\" y=\"59\" font-size=\"11\">45°</text></g></svg><br>केंद्र पर कोण = 2 × 45° = 90° → ΔOAB समकोण समद्विबाहु है<br>OM जीवा को समद्विभाजित करती है और \\(\\angle BOM = 45^\\circ\\), अतः OM = MB<br>d = OM = \\(\\frac{8}{2} = \\boxed{4}\\) cm<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (3): 4 cm है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":69,"local_id":"50069","quid":"Q1000071149","section":"MATH","topic":"Geometry","question":{"en":"In △ABC and △DEF, ∠A = 50°, ∠B = 60° and AB = DE. If ∠D = 50° and ∠E = 60°. By which property are △ABC and △DEF congruent? [SSC CGL 12/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"△ABC और △DEF में, ∠A = 50°, ∠B = 60° और AB = DE है। यदि ∠D = 50° और ∠E = 60° है, तो △ABC और △DEF किस गुण से सर्वांगसम हैं? [SSC CGL 12/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"SAS property","hi":"SAS गुण"},"2":{"en":"ASA property","hi":"ASA गुण"},"3":{"en":"SSS property","hi":"SSS गुण"},"4":{"en":"RHS property","hi":"RHS गुण"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<svg width=\"175\" height=\"128\" viewBox=\"0 0 175 128\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" font-size=\"12\"><path d=\"M96 20L25 105H145Z\"/><g fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\"><text x=\"96\" y=\"14\" text-anchor=\"middle\">C</text><text x=\"13\" y=\"109\">A</text><text x=\"149\" y=\"109\">B</text><text x=\"49\" y=\"98\" text-anchor=\"middle\">50°</text><text x=\"122\" y=\"97\" text-anchor=\"middle\">60°</text></g></svg>&nbsp; <svg width=\"175\" height=\"128\" viewBox=\"0 0 175 128\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" font-size=\"12\"><path d=\"M96 20L25 105H145Z\"/><g fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\"><text x=\"96\" y=\"14\" text-anchor=\"middle\">F</text><text x=\"13\" y=\"109\">D</text><text x=\"149\" y=\"109\">E</text><text x=\"49\" y=\"98\" text-anchor=\"middle\">50°</text><text x=\"122\" y=\"97\" text-anchor=\"middle\">60°</text></g></svg><br>∠A = ∠D = 50° (Angle)<br>AB = DE (included Side)<br>∠B = ∠E = 60° (Angle)<br>Two angles and the included side are equal → \\(\\boxed{\\text{ASA}}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): ASA property.</b>","hi":"<svg width=\"175\" height=\"128\" viewBox=\"0 0 175 128\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" font-size=\"12\"><path d=\"M96 20L25 105H145Z\"/><g fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\"><text x=\"96\" y=\"14\" text-anchor=\"middle\">C</text><text x=\"13\" y=\"109\">A</text><text x=\"149\" y=\"109\">B</text><text x=\"49\" y=\"98\" text-anchor=\"middle\">50°</text><text x=\"122\" y=\"97\" text-anchor=\"middle\">60°</text></g></svg>&nbsp; <svg width=\"175\" height=\"128\" viewBox=\"0 0 175 128\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" font-size=\"12\"><path d=\"M96 20L25 105H145Z\"/><g fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\"><text x=\"96\" y=\"14\" text-anchor=\"middle\">F</text><text x=\"13\" y=\"109\">D</text><text x=\"149\" y=\"109\">E</text><text x=\"49\" y=\"98\" text-anchor=\"middle\">50°</text><text x=\"122\" y=\"97\" text-anchor=\"middle\">60°</text></g></svg><br>∠A = ∠D = 50° (कोण)<br>AB = DE (बीच की भुजा)<br>∠B = ∠E = 60° (कोण)<br>दो कोण और उनके बीच की भुजा बराबर → \\(\\boxed{\\text{ASA}}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): ASA गुण है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":70,"local_id":"50070","quid":"Q1000071150","section":"MATH","topic":"Geometry","question":{"en":"Two identical circles, each of radius 8 cm, intersect so that the distance between their centres is equal to the radius. Find the length of their common chord. [SSC CGL 12/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"8 cm त्रिज्या वाले दो सर्वसम वृत्त इस प्रकार प्रतिच्छेद करते हैं कि उनके केंद्रों के बीच की दूरी त्रिज्या के बराबर है। उनकी उभयनिष्ठ जीवा की लंबाई ज्ञात कीजिए। [SSC CGL 12/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"4 cm"},"2":{"en":"\\(4\\sqrt{3}\\) cm"},"3":{"en":"8 cm"},"4":{"en":"\\(8\\sqrt{3}\\) cm"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"<svg width=\"190\" height=\"150\" viewBox=\"0 0 190 150\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" font-size=\"12\"><circle cx=\"70\" cy=\"75\" r=\"50\"/><circle cx=\"120\" cy=\"75\" r=\"50\"/><path d=\"M95 32V118\"/><path stroke-dasharray=\"4 3\" d=\"M70 75H120M70 75L95 32\"/><g fill=\"#000\"><circle cx=\"70\" cy=\"75\" r=\"1.5\"/><circle cx=\"120\" cy=\"75\" r=\"1.5\"/></g><g fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\"><text x=\"66\" y=\"89\" text-anchor=\"end\">O₁</text><text x=\"124\" y=\"89\">O₂</text><text x=\"95\" y=\"27\" text-anchor=\"middle\">A</text><text x=\"95\" y=\"132\" text-anchor=\"middle\">B</text><text x=\"76\" y=\"53\" text-anchor=\"end\">8</text><text x=\"107\" y=\"71\">M</text><text x=\"90\" y=\"89\" text-anchor=\"end\">8</text></g></svg><br>Common chord AB ⟂ O₁O₂ and bisects it → O₁M = 4 cm<br>AM = \\(\\sqrt{8^2 - 4^2} = \\sqrt{48} = 4\\sqrt{3}\\)<br>AB = \\(2 \\times 4\\sqrt{3} = \\boxed{8\\sqrt{3}}\\) cm<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): \\(8\\sqrt{3}\\) cm.</b>","hi":"<svg width=\"190\" height=\"150\" viewBox=\"0 0 190 150\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" font-size=\"12\"><circle cx=\"70\" cy=\"75\" r=\"50\"/><circle cx=\"120\" cy=\"75\" r=\"50\"/><path d=\"M95 32V118\"/><path stroke-dasharray=\"4 3\" d=\"M70 75H120M70 75L95 32\"/><g fill=\"#000\"><circle cx=\"70\" cy=\"75\" r=\"1.5\"/><circle cx=\"120\" cy=\"75\" r=\"1.5\"/></g><g fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\"><text x=\"66\" y=\"89\" text-anchor=\"end\">O₁</text><text x=\"124\" y=\"89\">O₂</text><text x=\"95\" y=\"27\" text-anchor=\"middle\">A</text><text x=\"95\" y=\"132\" text-anchor=\"middle\">B</text><text x=\"76\" y=\"53\" text-anchor=\"end\">8</text><text x=\"107\" y=\"71\">M</text><text x=\"90\" y=\"89\" text-anchor=\"end\">8</text></g></svg><br>उभयनिष्ठ जीवा AB, O₁O₂ पर लंब है और उसे समद्विभाजित करती है → O₁M = 4 cm<br>AM = \\(\\sqrt{8^2 - 4^2} = \\sqrt{48} = 4\\sqrt{3}\\)<br>AB = \\(2 \\times 4\\sqrt{3} = \\boxed{8\\sqrt{3}}\\) cm<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (4): \\(8\\sqrt{3}\\) cm है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":71,"local_id":"50071","quid":"Q1000071151","section":"MATH","topic":"Mixture and Alligation","question":{"en":"A dishonest milkman sells his mixture at the cost price and gains 60%. Find the percentage of water in the mixture. [SSC CGL 12/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"एक बेईमान दूधवाला अपना मिश्रण क्रय मूल्य पर बेचता है और 60% लाभ कमाता है। मिश्रण में पानी का प्रतिशत ज्ञात कीजिए। [SSC CGL 12/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"42.5%"},"2":{"en":"35%"},"3":{"en":"37.5%"},"4":{"en":"46%"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"Gain comes from water → Water : Milk = 60 : 100 = 3 : 5<br>Water % = \\(\\frac{3}{8} \\times 100 = \\boxed{37.5\\%}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): 37.5%.</b>","hi":"लाभ पानी से होता है → पानी : दूध = 60 : 100 = 3 : 5<br>पानी % = \\(\\frac{3}{8} \\times 100 = \\boxed{37.5\\%}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (3): 37.5% है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":72,"local_id":"50072","quid":"Q1000071152","section":"MATH","topic":"Elementary Statistics","question":{"en":"Read the given histogram carefully which shows the number of cars observed at different time intervals of the day (in hours) and answer the question that follows:<br>Find the time interval during which more than 20% of total cars passed.<br><img src=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-12-OCT-2026-SHIFT-3/q72.jpg\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\"> [SSC CGL 12/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"दिए गए आयतचित्र को ध्यानपूर्वक पढ़िए, जो दिन के विभिन्न समय अंतरालों (घंटों में) में देखी गई कारों की संख्या दर्शाता है, और नीचे दिए गए प्रश्न का उत्तर दीजिए:<br>वह समय अंतराल ज्ञात कीजिए जिसमें कुल कारों की 20% से अधिक कारें गुजरीं।<br><img src=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-12-OCT-2026-SHIFT-3/q72.jpg\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\"> [SSC CGL 12/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"9-10"},"2":{"en":"7-8"},"3":{"en":"10-11"},"4":{"en":"8-9"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"Cars: 70, 105, 128, 109, 97, 51<br>Total = 560 → 20% of 560 = 112<br>Only 128 \\(\\gt\\) 112 → interval \\(\\boxed{8 - 9}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): 8-9.</b>","hi":"कारें: 70, 105, 128, 109, 97, 51<br>कुल = 560 → 560 का 20% = 112<br>केवल 128 \\(\\gt\\) 112 → अंतराल \\(\\boxed{8 - 9}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (4): 8-9 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":true,"images":{"question":["https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-12-OCT-2026-SHIFT-3/q72.jpg"]}},{"no":73,"local_id":"50073","quid":"Q1000071153","section":"MATH","topic":"Geometry","question":{"en":"Two circles have centres P and Q with radii 6 cm and 3 cm, respectively. AC is a transverse common tangent touching the circles at points A and C. If AC intersects the line joining the centres PQ at point B, and AB = 8 cm, find the length of PQ. [SSC CGL 12/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"दो वृत्तों के केंद्र P और Q हैं तथा उनकी त्रिज्याएँ क्रमशः 6 cm और 3 cm हैं। AC एक अनुप्रस्थ उभयनिष्ठ स्पर्श रेखा है जो वृत्तों को A और C बिंदुओं पर स्पर्श करती है। यदि AC, केंद्रों को मिलाने वाली रेखा PQ को बिंदु B पर काटती है, और AB = 8 cm है, तो PQ की लंबाई ज्ञात कीजिए। [SSC CGL 12/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"12 cm"},"2":{"en":"15 cm"},"3":{"en":"18 cm"},"4":{"en":"21 cm"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<svg width=\"302\" height=\"177\" viewBox=\"0 0 302 177\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" font-size=\"12\"><path d=\"M114 29L241 125M88 88L126 38M245 88L226 114M122 43L127 47L131 42M230 109L225 105L221 110\"/><path stroke-dasharray=\"4 3\" d=\"M88 88L245 88\"/><circle cx=\"88\" cy=\"88\" r=\"62\"/><circle cx=\"245\" cy=\"88\" r=\"31\"/><circle cx=\"88\" cy=\"88\" r=\"2\" fill=\"#000\"/><circle cx=\"245\" cy=\"88\" r=\"2\" fill=\"#000\"/><circle cx=\"193\" cy=\"88\" r=\"2\" fill=\"#000\"/><g fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3\" paint-order=\"stroke\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" text-anchor=\"middle\"><text x=\"84\" y=\"99\">P</text><text x=\"249\" y=\"99\">Q</text><text x=\"124\" y=\"36\">A</text><text x=\"227\" y=\"124\">C</text><text x=\"202\" y=\"84\">B</text><text x=\"113\" y=\"72\">6</text><text x=\"229\" y=\"101\">3</text><text x=\"155\" y=\"73\">8</text></g></svg><br>PA ⟂ AB → PB = \\(\\sqrt{6^2 + 8^2} = 10\\) cm<br>ΔPAB ~ ΔQCB → \\(\\frac{PB}{QB} = \\frac{6}{3}\\) → QB = 5 cm<br>PQ = 10 + 5 = \\(\\boxed{15}\\) cm<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): 15 cm.</b>","hi":"<svg width=\"302\" height=\"177\" viewBox=\"0 0 302 177\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" font-size=\"12\"><path d=\"M114 29L241 125M88 88L126 38M245 88L226 114M122 43L127 47L131 42M230 109L225 105L221 110\"/><path stroke-dasharray=\"4 3\" d=\"M88 88L245 88\"/><circle cx=\"88\" cy=\"88\" r=\"62\"/><circle cx=\"245\" cy=\"88\" r=\"31\"/><circle cx=\"88\" cy=\"88\" r=\"2\" fill=\"#000\"/><circle cx=\"245\" cy=\"88\" r=\"2\" fill=\"#000\"/><circle cx=\"193\" cy=\"88\" r=\"2\" fill=\"#000\"/><g fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3\" paint-order=\"stroke\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" text-anchor=\"middle\"><text x=\"84\" y=\"99\">P</text><text x=\"249\" y=\"99\">Q</text><text x=\"124\" y=\"36\">A</text><text x=\"227\" y=\"124\">C</text><text x=\"202\" y=\"84\">B</text><text x=\"113\" y=\"72\">6</text><text x=\"229\" y=\"101\">3</text><text x=\"155\" y=\"73\">8</text></g></svg><br>PA ⟂ AB → PB = \\(\\sqrt{6^2 + 8^2} = 10\\) cm<br>ΔPAB ~ ΔQCB → \\(\\frac{PB}{QB} = \\frac{6}{3}\\) → QB = 5 cm<br>PQ = 10 + 5 = \\(\\boxed{15}\\) cm<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): 15 cm है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":74,"local_id":"50074","quid":"Q1000071154","section":"MATH","topic":"Data Interpretation (DI)","question":{"en":"The following pie-chart illustrates the percentage distribution of study time allocated to various subjects and activities. Study the pie-chart thoroughly and solve the questions based on the conditions provided.<br>Suppose a student's total study time is 40 hours per week. The student decides to increase the efficiency of 'Mathematics' by 20% (meaning they achieve the same learning output in 20% less time) and reallocates the \"saved\" time equally between 'Reasoning' and 'Revision'. What is the new absolute time (in minutes) spent on 'Reasoning'?<br><img src=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-12-OCT-2026-SHIFT-3/q74.jpg\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\"> [SSC CGL 12/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"निम्नलिखित पाई-चार्ट विभिन्न विषयों और गतिविधियों को दिए गए अध्ययन समय का प्रतिशत वितरण दर्शाता है। पाई-चार्ट का भली-भाँति अध्ययन कीजिए और दी गई शर्तों के आधार पर प्रश्नों को हल कीजिए।<br>मान लीजिए एक छात्र का कुल अध्ययन समय 40 घंटे प्रति सप्ताह है। छात्र 'गणित' की दक्षता 20% बढ़ाने का निर्णय लेता है (अर्थात वह 20% कम समय में समान सीखने का परिणाम प्राप्त करता है) और \"बचाए गए\" समय को 'रीज़निंग' और 'रिवीज़न' के बीच बराबर बाँट देता है। 'रीज़निंग' पर व्यतीत नया कुल समय (मिनटों में) क्या है?<br><img src=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-12-OCT-2026-SHIFT-3/q74.jpg\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\"> [SSC CGL 12/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"324 minutes","hi":"324 मिनट"},"2":{"en":"244 minutes","hi":"244 मिनट"},"3":{"en":"240 minutes","hi":"240 मिनट"},"4":{"en":"304 minutes","hi":"304 मिनट"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"Total = 40 hr = 2400 min. From the chart: Mathematics 35%, Reasoning 10%<br>Mathematics = 840 min; saved = 20% of 840 = 168 min<br>Reasoning gets \\(\\frac{168}{2} = 84\\) min more<br>Reasoning = 240 + 84 = \\(\\boxed{324}\\) min<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): 324 minutes.</b>","hi":"कुल = 40 घंटे = 2400 मिनट. चार्ट से: गणित 35%, रीज़निंग 10%<br>गणित = 840 मिनट; बचत = 840 का 20% = 168 मिनट<br>रीज़निंग को \\(\\frac{168}{2} = 84\\) मिनट अधिक मिलते हैं<br>रीज़निंग = 240 + 84 = \\(\\boxed{324}\\) मिनट<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (1): 324 मिनट है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":true,"images":{"question":["https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-12-OCT-2026-SHIFT-3/q74.jpg"]}},{"no":75,"local_id":"50075","quid":"Q1000071155","section":"MATH","topic":"Percentage","question":{"en":"A technology incubator filters down an initial cohort of tech startups over a multi-stage funding cycle.<br>• In the first screening phase, 30% of the total startups are eliminated.<br>• In the second phase, 25% of the remaining startups fail to build a viable prototype and are dropped.<br>• In the final venture round, 20% of the then-remaining startups are rejected due to compliance errors.<br>If exactly 42 startups successfully clear all three evaluation stages and secure institutional funding, how many startups were in the initial incubator cohort? [SSC CGL 12/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"एक प्रौद्योगिकी इनक्यूबेटर बहु-चरणीय फंडिंग चक्र में टेक स्टार्टअप्स के प्रारंभिक समूह को छाँटता है।<br>• पहले स्क्रीनिंग चरण में, कुल स्टार्टअप्स में से 30% बाहर कर दिए जाते हैं।<br>• दूसरे चरण में, शेष स्टार्टअप्स में से 25% व्यवहार्य प्रोटोटाइप नहीं बना पाते और हटा दिए जाते हैं।<br>• अंतिम वेंचर राउंड में, तब शेष स्टार्टअप्स में से 20% अनुपालन त्रुटियों के कारण अस्वीकार कर दिए जाते हैं।<br>यदि ठीक 42 स्टार्टअप तीनों मूल्यांकन चरण सफलतापूर्वक पार करके संस्थागत फंडिंग प्राप्त करते हैं, तो इनक्यूबेटर के प्रारंभिक समूह में कितने स्टार्टअप थे? [SSC CGL 12/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"100"},"2":{"en":"90"},"3":{"en":"110"},"4":{"en":"150"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"Remaining = \\(N \\times \\frac{70}{100} \\times \\frac{75}{100} \\times \\frac{80}{100} = 0.42N\\)<br>\\(0.42N = 42\\)<br>\\(N = \\boxed{100}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): 100.</b>","hi":"शेष = \\(N \\times \\frac{70}{100} \\times \\frac{75}{100} \\times \\frac{80}{100} = 0.42N\\)<br>\\(0.42N = 42\\)<br>\\(N = \\boxed{100}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (1): 100 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false}]},"ENGLISH":{"seconds":900,"questions":[{"no":76,"local_id":"50076","quid":"Q1000071156","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Direct Indirect (Narration)","question":{"en":"Choose the appropriate direct speech from the given sentence.<br>She forbade me to go with him. [SSC CGL 12/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"She said, “Don't go with him.”"},"2":{"en":"She said, “You should not go with him.”"},"3":{"en":"She said, “Go with him.”"},"4":{"en":"She said, “You must not go with him.”"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<b>Rule: “Forbade + object + infinitive” reports a direct negative command.</b><br>The original words are therefore “Don’t go with him.”<br>B weakens the prohibition to advice; C reverses the meaning.<br>D expresses necessity rather than the direct imperative used by the speaker.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): She said, “Don't go with him.”.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":77,"local_id":"50077","quid":"Q1000071157","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Direct Indirect (Narration)","question":{"en":"Choose the correct indirect speech form of the following sentence.<br>She said, “Do you like mangoes?” [SSC CGL 12/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"She asked me if I liked mangoes."},"2":{"en":"She said if I like mangoes."},"3":{"en":"She asked me do I like mangoes."},"4":{"en":"She told me that I liked mangoes."}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<b>Rule: Yes/no questions use “asked + object + if,” statement order and backshifted tense.</b><br>“Do you like” becomes “if I liked.”<br>B uses “said” and retains the present; C retains direct question structure.<br>D changes the question into a statement.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): She asked me if I liked mangoes.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":78,"local_id":"50078","quid":"Q1000071158","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Fill in the Blanks","question":{"en":"Fill in the blank with appropriate parts of speech.<br>The soldiers, exhausted though they were, pressed on with an almost ___ fortitude. [SSC CGL 12/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"mechanical"},"2":{"en":"mechanically"},"3":{"en":"mechanize"},"4":{"en":"mechanic"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<b>Rule: An adjective modifies the noun “fortitude.”</b><br>“Mechanical” describes an automatic, unthinking display of endurance.<br>“Mechanically” is an adverb, “mechanize” is a verb, and “mechanic” is a noun.<br>Only “mechanical” fits the noun phrase.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): mechanical.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":79,"local_id":"50079","quid":"Q1000071159","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Para Jumbles (PQRS)","question":{"en":"Rearrange the parts of the sentence in the correct order.<br>The recent diplomatic summit<br>P. and fostering regional cooperation<br>Q. witnessed discussions on security concerns<br>R. while addressing climate change policies,<br>S. aimed at strengthening bilateral trade [SSC CGL 12/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"PQRS"},"2":{"en":"QSRP"},"3":{"en":"QRSP"},"4":{"en":"PRSQ"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Order: QRSP</b><br>Q supplies the main predicate: the summit witnessed security discussions.<br>R adds climate policy as another topic.<br>S and P give the linked goals of bilateral trade and regional cooperation.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): QRSP.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":80,"local_id":"50080","quid":"Q1000071160","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Idioms and Phrases","question":{"en":"Choose the correct idiom for the word highlighted in bold.<br>The two famous writers <b>crossed swords</b> with each other on every issue. [SSC CGL 12/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Became good friends"},"2":{"en":"Engaged in a heated argument"},"3":{"en":"Collaborated on a project"},"4":{"en":"Ignored each other"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Cross swords (तर्क-वितर्क में उलझना) = engage in a heated dispute.</b><br>The writers argued about every issue.<br>Example: “The critics crossed swords over the novel’s meaning.”<br>Friendship, collaboration and ignoring one another contradict the idiom.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): Engaged in a heated argument.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":81,"local_id":"50081","quid":"Q1000071161","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Idioms and Phrases","question":{"en":"What does the idiom “To take to one's heels” mean? [SSC CGL 12/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"To start running away quickly"},"2":{"en":"To wear new shoes"},"3":{"en":"To stand still in fear"},"4":{"en":"To take a rest after a long walk"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<b>Take to one’s heels (भाग निकलना) = run away quickly.</b><br>Example: “The thief took to his heels when the police arrived.”<br>Wearing shoes, standing still and resting do not describe flight.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): To start running away quickly.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":82,"local_id":"50082","quid":"Q1000071162","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Sentence Improvement","question":{"en":"Improve the sentence by choosing the correct degree of comparison that replaces the words highlighted in bold.<br>This is the <b>borest</b> movie I have ever seen. [SSC CGL 12/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"more boring"},"2":{"en":"boring"},"3":{"en":"most boring"},"4":{"en":"boringest"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Rule: “Boring” forms its superlative as “most boring.”</b><br>The phrase “I have ever seen” compares the film with an entire set, so the superlative is required.<br>Correct sentence: “This is the <b>most boring</b> movie I have ever seen.”<br>“Borest” and “boringest” are nonstandard; “more boring” is comparative.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): most boring.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":83,"local_id":"50083","quid":"Q1000071163","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Spotting Errors","question":{"en":"Identify the error in the sentence.<br>I have a strongly feeling that something's off. [SSC CGL 12/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"feeling"},"2":{"en":"strongly"},"3":{"en":"have"},"4":{"en":"something"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Rule: An adjective modifies the noun “feeling.”</b><br>“Strongly” is an adverb and must become “strong.”<br>Correct sentence: “I have a <b>strong</b> feeling that something’s off.”<br>The remaining parts are correct.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): strongly.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":84,"local_id":"50084","quid":"Q1000071164","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Homophones and Homonyms","question":{"en":"Which of the following options is TRUE about the underlined word?<br>The debate over climate change is <u>moot</u> since the policy has already been enacted. [SSC CGL 12/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"The word “moot” is incorrectly used here. The word “mute” should be used instead."},"2":{"en":"The word “moot” is incorrectly used here. The word “mote” should be used instead."},"3":{"en":"The word “moot” is incorrectly used here. The word “moat” should be used instead."},"4":{"en":"The word “moot” is correctly used here."}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"<b>Moot (विवाद के बाद अप्रासंगिक) = no longer relevant or open to practical decision.</b><br>Since the policy has already been enacted, the debate has become academic or irrelevant.<br>“Mute” means silent, “mote” means a tiny particle, and “moat” means a defensive ditch.<br>Therefore, “moot” is correctly used.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): The word “moot” is correctly used here.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":85,"local_id":"50085","quid":"Q1000071165","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Spelling Check","question":{"en":"Fill in the blank with the correctly spelt word.<br>The climate model is still ___ due to limited data. [SSC CGL 12/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"specullative"},"2":{"en":"speculative"},"3":{"en":"specculative"},"4":{"en":"speculattive"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Speculative (अनुमानित) = based on conjecture rather than firm evidence.</b><br>The correct spelling is “speculative.”<br><b>Specullative</b> doubles “l”; <b>specculative</b> doubles “c.”<br><b>Speculattive</b> doubles “t.”<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): speculative.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":86,"local_id":"50086","quid":"Q1000071166","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Antonym","question":{"en":"Select the most appropriate antonym of the given word. <b>Gregarious</b> [SSC CGL 12/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Social"},"2":{"en":"Reserved"},"3":{"en":"Friendly"},"4":{"en":"Outgoing"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Gregarious (मिलनसार) = fond of company and sociable.</b><br><b>Social (सामाजिक)</b> = enjoying interaction<br><b>Reserved (संकोची)</b> = slow to reveal feelings or mix freely ✔<br><b>Friendly (मिलनसार)</b> = kind and approachable<br><b>Outgoing (खुला-मिलनसार)</b> = socially confident<br>More antonyms: withdrawn, reclusive, unsociable.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): Reserved.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":87,"local_id":"50087","quid":"Q1000071167","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Spelling Check","question":{"en":"Spot the correct spelling of a word for long-winded style. [SSC CGL 12/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Sesquipidalian"},"2":{"en":"Sesquipedelian"},"3":{"en":"Sesquipedalian"},"4":{"en":"Sesquipadalian"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Sesquipedalian (दीर्घ शब्दों का) = characterized by long words or long-winded language.</b><br>The correct sequence is “sesqui-ped-alian.”<br><b>Sesquipidalian</b> replaces “e” with “i”; <b>sesquipedelian</b> omits “a.”<br><b>Sesquipadalian</b> replaces “e” with “a.”<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): Sesquipedalian.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":88,"local_id":"50088","quid":"Q1000071168","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Spelling Check","question":{"en":"Identify the misspelt word. [SSC CGL 12/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Recalcitrant"},"2":{"en":"Perspicuity"},"3":{"en":"Superfluous"},"4":{"en":"Prophane"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"<b>Profane (अपवित्र) = secular or disrespectful toward sacred things.</b><br><b>Prophane</b> wrongly inserts “h”; the correct spelling is “profane.”<br><b>Recalcitrant (उद्दंड)</b> = stubbornly disobedient; spelling correct.<br><b>Perspicuity (स्पष्टता)</b> = clarity; <b>superfluous (अनावश्यक)</b> = unnecessary.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): Prophane.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":89,"local_id":"50089","quid":"Q1000071169","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"One Word Substitution","question":{"en":"Choose the correct one-word substitute for: “Something that cannot be explained or understood”. [SSC CGL 12/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"illegible"},"2":{"en":"Incredible"},"3":{"en":"inexplicable"},"4":{"en":"indelible"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Inexplicable (अव्याख्येय) = impossible to explain or understand.</b><br><b>Illegible (अपठनीय)</b> = impossible to read<br><b>Incredible (अविश्वसनीय)</b> = difficult to believe<br><b>Indelible (अमिट)</b> = impossible to erase<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): inexplicable.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":90,"local_id":"50090","quid":"Q1000071170","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"One Word Substitution","question":{"en":"Choose the correct one-word substitute for: “Something mysterious or difficult to understand”. [SSC CGL 12/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Enchant"},"2":{"en":"Enigma"},"3":{"en":"Meme"},"4":{"en":"Riddle"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Enigma (पहेली, रहस्य) = a mysterious person, thing or situation.</b><br><b>Enchant (मोहित करना)</b> = delight or cast a spell<br><b>Meme (मीम)</b> = an idea or image spread through a culture<br><b>Riddle (पहेली)</b> = a puzzle, but “enigma” better describes an enduring mystery<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): Enigma.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":91,"local_id":"50091","quid":"Q1000071171","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Spotting Errors","question":{"en":"Find the part of the sentence that contains an error:<br>What critics often overlook (1)/ is not the literary structure per se, (2)/ but the emotional authenticity of characters (3)/ and how it affects reader's trust. (4) [SSC CGL 12/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"(1)"},"2":{"en":"(2)"},"3":{"en":"(3)"},"4":{"en":"(4)"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"<b>Rule: Use the plural possessive when referring to readers generally.</b><br>Part (4) should read “readers’ trust,” with the apostrophe after the plural “s.”<br>The singular “reader’s trust” does not fit the general reference.<br>The remaining parts are grammatically sound.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): (4).</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":92,"local_id":"50092","quid":"Q1000071172","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Homophones and Homonyms","question":{"en":"Select the sentence containing the homonym of the highlighted word:<br>The ethnographer noted the <b>fetish</b> worshipped by the tribe. [SSC CGL 12/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"The tourist purchased a tribal fetish as a souvenir."},"2":{"en":"The historian discussed colonial views on fetish objects."},"3":{"en":"The novel explored a character's shoe fetish."},"4":{"en":"The anthropologist documented a carved fetish near the shrine."}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Fetish: an object of religious worship; also an excessive fixation or sexual attraction.</b><br>The original sentence uses the anthropological religious sense.<br>Option 3 uses it for a character’s fixation on shoes, a different meaning.<br>Options 1, 2 and 4 retain the cultural-object sense.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): The novel explored a character's shoe fetish.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":93,"local_id":"50093","quid":"Q1000071173","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Sentence Improvement","question":{"en":"Choose the most suitable option to replace the highlighted part of the sentence:<br>He <b>is used to work</b> hard every day. [SSC CGL 12/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"used to working hard"},"2":{"en":"is used to working hard"},"3":{"en":"used to work hardly"},"4":{"en":"uses to working hard"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Rule: “Be used to + gerund” means be accustomed to doing something.</b><br>Correct sentence: “He <b>is used to working</b> hard every day.”<br>A omits “is”; C changes the meaning with “hardly,” meaning scarcely.<br>D uses the incorrect form “uses to.”<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): is used to working hard.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":94,"local_id":"50094","quid":"Q1000071174","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Direct Indirect (Narration)","question":{"en":"A sentence is provided in direct speech. From the four given options, choose the one that most accurately conveys the sentence in its corresponding indirect speech.<br>He said, “I must finish this work.” [SSC CGL 12/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"He said that he must finish that work."},"2":{"en":"He said that he had to finish this work."},"3":{"en":"He said that he had to finish that work."},"4":{"en":"He said that he has to finish that work."}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Rule: “Must” expressing necessity becomes “had to,” and “this” becomes “that.”</b><br>“I” changes to “he.”<br>A retains “must”; B retains “this”; D uses present “has to.”<br>C makes all required changes.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): He said that he had to finish that work.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":95,"local_id":"50095","quid":"Q1000071175","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Para Jumbles (PQRS)","question":{"en":"Rearrange the following sentences to form a coherent paragraph:<br>1. This phenomenon, where the physical state of a substance changes without a change in temperature, is a result of the absorption or release of latent heat.<br>2. When a solid, such as ice, melts, its temperature remains constant at 0°C until all of the ice has turned to water.<br>3. This energy is used to break the molecular bonds of the solid, rather than increasing the kinetic energy of the molecules.<br>4. The concept of latent heat is crucial for understanding phase transitions in thermodynamics. [SSC CGL 12/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"4,2,1,3"},"2":{"en":"2,1,4,3"},"3":{"en":"1,3,2,4"},"4":{"en":"3,1,2,4"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<b>Order: 4-2-1-3</b><br>Sentence 4 introduces latent heat and phase transitions.<br>Sentence 2 gives the melting-ice example, and sentence 1 explains the phenomenon through latent heat.<br>Sentence 3 concludes by explaining how “this energy” is used.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): 4,2,1,3.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":96,"local_id":"50096","quid":"Q1000071176","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Cloze Test","question":{"en":"Complete the following passage by filling in the blanks with the most appropriate words from the options given below.<br><br>The growing use of virtual reality (VR) in education reflects a shift in how knowledge is constructed and internalised. Unlike conventional media, immersive environments allow learners to engage directly with abstract concepts. Educational psychologists argue that such experiences help learners build mental models that are more readily (A)___ into long-term memory than information gained through lectures or textbooks.<br><br>However, immersion alone does not ensure intellectual progress. A visually impressive simulation may attract attention without promoting conceptual understanding. Thus, VR depends on technological sophistication and pedagogical frameworks that (B)___ learners’ cognitive limitations while encouraging analytical reflection. Realistic simulations may improve motivation, but excessive sensory information can overwhelm learners. Researchers therefore recommend structured pauses for reflection, (C)___ students confuse vivid experiences with durable understanding.<br><br>VR raises concerns about access. Wealthier institutions are more likely to adopt advanced technologies than those with limited budgets. (D)___ technological capability continues to expand, disparities in educational access remain persistent. Ultimately, VR will fulfil its educational promise only through thoughtful design and equitable implementation. Otherwise, its initial appeal may gradually (E)___ leaving impressive technology but limited educational transformation.<br><br><br>Which word most appropriately fills blank (A) to convey the process by which newly acquired knowledge becomes deeply integrated into a learner's long-term cognitive framework? [SSC CGL 12/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"assimilated"},"2":{"en":"fabricated"},"3":{"en":"accumulated"},"4":{"en":"inherited"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<b>Assimilated (आत्मसात किया गया) = absorbed and integrated into existing knowledge.</b><br>Mental models are assimilated into long-term memory.<br><b>Fabricated (गढ़ा गया)</b> = invented falsely<br><b>Accumulated (संचित)</b> = gathered; <b>inherited (विरासत में मिला)</b> = received from predecessors<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): assimilated.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":97,"local_id":"50097","quid":"Q1000071177","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Cloze Test","question":{"en":"Complete the following passage by filling in the blanks with the most appropriate words from the options given below.<br><br>The growing use of virtual reality (VR) in education reflects a shift in how knowledge is constructed and internalised. Unlike conventional media, immersive environments allow learners to engage directly with abstract concepts. Educational psychologists argue that such experiences help learners build mental models that are more readily (A)___ into long-term memory than information gained through lectures or textbooks.<br><br>However, immersion alone does not ensure intellectual progress. A visually impressive simulation may attract attention without promoting conceptual understanding. Thus, VR depends on technological sophistication and pedagogical frameworks that (B)___ learners’ cognitive limitations while encouraging analytical reflection. Realistic simulations may improve motivation, but excessive sensory information can overwhelm learners. Researchers therefore recommend structured pauses for reflection, (C)___ students confuse vivid experiences with durable understanding.<br><br>VR raises concerns about access. Wealthier institutions are more likely to adopt advanced technologies than those with limited budgets. (D)___ technological capability continues to expand, disparities in educational access remain persistent. Ultimately, VR will fulfil its educational promise only through thoughtful design and equitable implementation. Otherwise, its initial appeal may gradually (E)___ leaving impressive technology but limited educational transformation.<br><br><br>Which verb best fills blank (B), reflecting the idea that effective instructional design must take learners' mental capacities into careful consideration rather than ignore them? [SSC CGL 12/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Undermine"},"2":{"en":"intensify"},"3":{"en":"accommodate"},"4":{"en":"surpass"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Accommodate (अनुकूल बनाना) = take account of and adapt to needs or limitations.</b><br>Pedagogical frameworks should accommodate cognitive limitations.<br><b>Undermine (कमजोर करना)</b> = weaken<br><b>Intensify (तीव्र करना)</b> = increase; <b>surpass (पार करना)</b> = exceed<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): accommodate.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":98,"local_id":"50098","quid":"Q1000071178","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Cloze Test","question":{"en":"Complete the following passage by filling in the blanks with the most appropriate words from the options given below.<br><br>The growing use of virtual reality (VR) in education reflects a shift in how knowledge is constructed and internalised. Unlike conventional media, immersive environments allow learners to engage directly with abstract concepts. Educational psychologists argue that such experiences help learners build mental models that are more readily (A)___ into long-term memory than information gained through lectures or textbooks.<br><br>However, immersion alone does not ensure intellectual progress. A visually impressive simulation may attract attention without promoting conceptual understanding. Thus, VR depends on technological sophistication and pedagogical frameworks that (B)___ learners’ cognitive limitations while encouraging analytical reflection. Realistic simulations may improve motivation, but excessive sensory information can overwhelm learners. Researchers therefore recommend structured pauses for reflection, (C)___ students confuse vivid experiences with durable understanding.<br><br>VR raises concerns about access. Wealthier institutions are more likely to adopt advanced technologies than those with limited budgets. (D)___ technological capability continues to expand, disparities in educational access remain persistent. Ultimately, VR will fulfil its educational promise only through thoughtful design and equitable implementation. Otherwise, its initial appeal may gradually (E)___ leaving impressive technology but limited educational transformation.<br><br><br>Which conjunction most effectively fills blank (C) to express the preventive purpose behind providing opportunities for reflective thinking after immersive experiences? [SSC CGL 12/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"whereas"},"2":{"en":"lest"},"3":{"en":"whereby"},"4":{"en":"Notwithstanding"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Lest (ताकि … नहीं) introduces a preventive purpose.</b><br>Pauses are recommended lest students confuse vivid experiences with durable understanding.<br>“Whereas” expresses contrast; “whereby” expresses method.<br>“Notwithstanding” is a preposition or concessive connector, not the required conjunction.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): lest.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":99,"local_id":"50099","quid":"Q1000071179","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Cloze Test","question":{"en":"Complete the following passage by filling in the blanks with the most appropriate words from the options given below.<br><br>The growing use of virtual reality (VR) in education reflects a shift in how knowledge is constructed and internalised. Unlike conventional media, immersive environments allow learners to engage directly with abstract concepts. Educational psychologists argue that such experiences help learners build mental models that are more readily (A)___ into long-term memory than information gained through lectures or textbooks.<br><br>However, immersion alone does not ensure intellectual progress. A visually impressive simulation may attract attention without promoting conceptual understanding. Thus, VR depends on technological sophistication and pedagogical frameworks that (B)___ learners’ cognitive limitations while encouraging analytical reflection. Realistic simulations may improve motivation, but excessive sensory information can overwhelm learners. Researchers therefore recommend structured pauses for reflection, (C)___ students confuse vivid experiences with durable understanding.<br><br>VR raises concerns about access. Wealthier institutions are more likely to adopt advanced technologies than those with limited budgets. (D)___ technological capability continues to expand, disparities in educational access remain persistent. Ultimately, VR will fulfil its educational promise only through thoughtful design and equitable implementation. Otherwise, its initial appeal may gradually (E)___ leaving impressive technology but limited educational transformation.<br><br><br>Which connector best fills blank (D) to highlight the contrast between rapid technological advancement and the continued persistence of unequal educational opportunities? [SSC CGL 12/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Since"},"2":{"en":"Although"},"3":{"en":"Therefore"},"4":{"en":"Because"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Although (यद्यपि) introduces the required contrast.</b><br>Technological capability expands, although unequal educational access persists.<br>“Since” and “because” indicate cause, while “therefore” indicates result.<br>Only “although” expresses the opposition.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): Although.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":100,"local_id":"50100","quid":"Q1000071180","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Cloze Test","question":{"en":"Complete the following passage by filling in the blanks with the most appropriate words from the options given below.<br><br>The growing use of virtual reality (VR) in education reflects a shift in how knowledge is constructed and internalised. Unlike conventional media, immersive environments allow learners to engage directly with abstract concepts. Educational psychologists argue that such experiences help learners build mental models that are more readily (A)___ into long-term memory than information gained through lectures or textbooks.<br><br>However, immersion alone does not ensure intellectual progress. A visually impressive simulation may attract attention without promoting conceptual understanding. Thus, VR depends on technological sophistication and pedagogical frameworks that (B)___ learners’ cognitive limitations while encouraging analytical reflection. Realistic simulations may improve motivation, but excessive sensory information can overwhelm learners. Researchers therefore recommend structured pauses for reflection, (C)___ students confuse vivid experiences with durable understanding.<br><br>VR raises concerns about access. Wealthier institutions are more likely to adopt advanced technologies than those with limited budgets. (D)___ technological capability continues to expand, disparities in educational access remain persistent. Ultimately, VR will fulfil its educational promise only through thoughtful design and equitable implementation. Otherwise, its initial appeal may gradually (E)___ leaving impressive technology but limited educational transformation.<br><br><br>Which verb most accurately fills blank (E) to describe the gradual decline of public enthusiasm if educational innovation fails to produce meaningful outcomes? [SSC CGL 12/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"proliferate"},"2":{"en":"culminate"},"3":{"en":"subside"},"4":{"en":"intensify"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Subside (क्षीण होना) = gradually become less intense.</b><br>Initial enthusiasm may subside if VR produces little educational transformation.<br><b>Proliferate (तेजी से बढ़ना)</b> = multiply<br><b>Culminate (परिणति तक पहुँचना)</b> = reach a climax; <b>intensify (तीव्र होना)</b> = grow stronger<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): subside.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false}]}}};